"/><path d="M0 136L96 118H106L22 160H0Z" fill="#91592b"/><path d="M0 156L22 160L0 170Z" fill="#87a570"/><path d="M14 140L102 120" fill="none" stroke="#d4894a" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M10 150L60 138M30 154L84 132" fill="none" stroke="#d9b48a" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><rect x="92" y="118" width="4" height="16" fill="#2a3040"/><rect x="40" y="136" width="4" height="18" fill="#2a3040"/><rect x="70" y="128" width="4" height="18" fill="#2a3040"/><path d="M46 134L130 66" fill="none" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M130 66Q150 92 152 124" fill="none" stroke="#5c6b78" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><circle cx="152" cy="125" r="3.5" fill="#c4783a"/><path d="M148.5 125a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 7 0Z" fill="#fbf8f2"/><rect x="54" y="140" width="16" height="10" rx="2" fill="#80b1bc"/><rect x="54" y="140" width="16" height="3" rx="1" fill="#fbf8f2"/><path d="M206 150V112M214 152V104M222 150V116M198 152V120" fill="none" stroke="#6f8f5f" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><ellipse cx="214" cy="104" rx="2.6" ry="7" fill="#91592b"/><ellipse cx="206" cy="112" rx="2.4" ry="6" fill="#91592b"/><ellipse cx="222" cy="116" rx="2.4" ry="6" fill="#91592b"/><path d="M196 152q8 -22 2 -40M228 154q-6 -18 0 -34" fill="none" stroke="#87a570" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><strong>Fishing</strong><span class="c3ph-t">Ponds where you and your guests fish and let the fish go. You cannot swim or take a boat in the ponds.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">There is also line dancing, a coffee group and a craft fair.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-are-the-homes-like-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The homes">What are the homes like in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most homes in Myrtle Trace are one-story houses with their own yards, and a few are townhouses. Most were built in the 1980s and 1990s.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most have 3 bedrooms and about 1,500 to 2,100 square feet. The houses are on curving streets among trees and ponds, with Burning Ridge Golf Club next door. Wide paths between the houses are open to every resident.</p><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Myrtle Trace from above, with its edge drawn in orange: houses among tall pines and ponds, the clubhouse and main entrance marked, and the golf course next door" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Myrtle Trace from above, with the golf course next door. The orange line is the edge of the neighborhood.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-homes-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-homes-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-homes-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Houses with dark roofs, green yards and trees along two curving streets and a pond in Myrtle Trace, seen from above" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses along two streets and a pond in Myrtle Trace, from above.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some homes look out on the golf course, which is privately owned. Golf balls from the course can land in those yards.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each owner takes care of the house and the yard, including the roof and the grass.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the list of Myrtle Trace homes for sale.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us what you are looking for, and one of our agents will send you the homes for sale now.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-is-conway-like"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Conway">What is Conway like?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway is the town next to Myrtle Trace, on the Waccamaw River. Main Street in Conway is about 10 minutes away by car. Conway's riverwalk is a wooden boardwalk along the water, shaded by trees.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden boardwalk with a black railing, shaded by trees, beside old wooden buildings in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The riverwalk in Conway.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Main Street is lined with old brick buildings with shops and places to eat.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-main-street-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-main-street-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-main-street-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Main Street in downtown Conway, South Carolina, lined with old brick shop buildings" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>Main Street in Conway.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-does-it-cost-to-live-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Costs">What does it cost to live in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes in Myrtle Trace usually sell for about $300,000. If you live in the home, plan for these costs:</p><ul role="list" style="list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(13rem,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px"><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">HOA fee</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">$95 a month</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Property tax</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">About $1,200 a year</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">When you buy</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">A one-time fee to the HOA of a little over $1,500</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA uses the fee to keep up the pool, the clubhouse, the gates, the roads it owns, the ponds and the shared land. Myrtle Trace has a Conway address but is outside the city limits, so you pay no Conway city tax.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You probably will not need flood insurance, because no home here is in a high-risk flood zone on <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=101%20Myrtle%20Trace%20Drive%2C%20Conway%2C%20SC%2029526" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the government's flood map</a>. If you want it, a policy here usually costs about $550 a year.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get an insurance quote before you offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Pick the Myrtle Trace home you like. An agent at Chapter3 helps you get a homeowners <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">insurance</a> quote before you write the offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get a quote</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="who-can-live-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who can live here">Who can live in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At least one person in every home in Myrtle Trace must be 55 or older, under the <a href="https://myrtletracesc.org/wp-content/uploads/Guidelines/MyrtleTraceCovenant.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HOA's rules</a>. The others in the home can be any age, and grandchildren can visit.</p><style>main#main .mt-rules{list-style:none;margin:1.1rem 0 1.4rem;padding:0;max-width:720px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)}main#main .mt-rules li{display:flex;gap:.8rem;align-items:flex-start;margin:0;padding:.85rem 0 .9rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16);line-height:1.55}main#main .mt-rules .i{flex:0 0 auto;display:flex;color:var(--brass-ink);padding-top:.15rem}main#main .mt-rules strong{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;line-height:1.35;margin-bottom:.15rem}main#main .mt-rules span.t{display:block;color:var(--muted)}</style><ul role="list" class="mt-rules"><li><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 13c-2.5 0-5 2.6-5 5 0 1.6 1.2 2.5 2.6 2.5.9 0 1.6-.5 2.4-.5s1.5.5 2.4.5c1.4 0 2.6-.9 2.6-2.5 0-2.4-2.5-5-5-5z"/><circle cx="5.3" cy="11" r="1.8"/><circle cx="9" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="15" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="18.7" cy="11" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><strong>Pets</strong><span class="t">Yes. Keep them on a leash outside your yard, and out of the clubhouse and pool area.</span></span></li><li><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Renting it out</strong><span class="t">Yes, for a year or longer. One tenant must be 55 or older and live there.</span></span></li><li><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Sheds and pools</strong><span class="t">No free-standing sheds, gazebos or private swimming pools.</span></span></li><li><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><strong>Trucks and boats</strong><span class="t">Park your truck in the garage. Campers, boats and RVs can park at the clubhouse lot with a permit.</span></span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience, many HOAs here do not allow renting at all. Myrtle Trace does.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-does-myrtle-trace-compare-with-other-55-neighborhoods"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Compare">How does Myrtle Trace compare with other 55+ neighborhoods?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Trace has the lowest HOA fee of these four 55+ neighborhoods, and its homes usually sell for the least.</p><style>.c3-cmp tr.c3-self td{background:#fff;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy)!important}@media (max-width:599px){.c3-cmp tr.c3-self{background:#fff;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cmp tr.c3-self td{background:transparent}}@media (max-width:599px){.c3-cmp table,.c3-cmp tbody,.c3-cmp tr,.c3-cmp td{display:block;width:100%}.c3-cmp thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)}.c3-cmp tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .75rem;padding:.4rem 0}.c3-cmp td{border:0!important;padding:.25rem .9rem!important}.c3-cmp td:first-child{color:var(--navy)!important;font-weight:500;font-size:1rem}.c3-cmp td[data-label]:not(:first-child)::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy)}.c3-cmp td a{padding:11px 0}}</style><div class="c3-cmp" style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Community</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Area</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Minutes to the beach by car</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">HOA fee a month</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Resale homes usually sell for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">North Myrtle Beach</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $315</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $535,000</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb at Grande Dunes</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $400 for a house</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $665,000 for a house</td></tr><tr class="c3-self"><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:700">Myrtle Trace</strong></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 15</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$95</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $300,000</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Seasons at Prince Creek West</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Murrells Inlet</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $340</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $500,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-are-the-pros-and-cons-of-living-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Trace is minutes from the hospital and has a busy club calendar, and its homes are older.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The HOA fee is $95 a month. The HOA uses it to keep up the pool, clubhouse, gates, roads and ponds.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The hospital and a Walmart Supercenter are each about 3 minutes away by car.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Bingo, game nights, a Labor Day picnic and a craft fair are on the calendar.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The beach is about 15 minutes away by car.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Most homes were built in the 1980s and 1990s. <span class="c3-pc-do">Ask how old the roof is before you make an offer.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>There are no sidewalks.</span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="can-you-fence-a-yard-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Fences">Can you fence a yard in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually not in Myrtle Trace. Fences between yards and across the front are not allowed, and most lots cannot have a fence around the back yard either. A dog run is allowed once the HOA approves it.</p><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> Pat is moving from Erie, Pennsylvania, with her dog, Max, and she wants a fenced back yard where he can run. She likes a house in Myrtle Trace that backs onto the golf course.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Before she makes an offer, her Chapter3 agent reads the neighborhood's rules with her. A house on the golf course cannot have a fence around its back yard.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">The agent shows her that a dog run, a small pen beside the house, is allowed once the HOA approves it. Pat makes her offer, with a plan for Max's dog run beside the patio.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An agent at Chapter3 can <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">read the HOA's rules with you</a> before you make an offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="myrtle-trace-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Myrtle Trace FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Trace a gated community?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only in part. The front entrance is always open. The HOA put gates on the back entrance so drivers do not cut through the neighborhood.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is the HOA fee in Myrtle Trace?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA fee is $95 a month. The HOA uses it to keep up the pool, the clubhouse, the gates, the roads it owns, the ponds and the shared land.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Trace South part of Myrtle Trace?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Myrtle Trace South and Myrtle Trace Grande are separate neighborhoods, each with its own HOA. The fee and rules on this page are for Myrtle Trace.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who runs the Myrtle Trace HOA?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The owners run the Myrtle Trace HOA themselves, with volunteers. There is no management company.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is the golf course part of Myrtle Trace?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Burning Ridge Golf Club, next door, is privately owned and is not part of the HOA. Some Myrtle Trace homes back onto it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you fish in the Myrtle Trace ponds?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Residents and their house guests can fish from the shared land around the 15 ponds. You let every fish go.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do you need flood insurance in Myrtle Trace?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Probably not. No home here is in a high-risk flood zone. If you want a policy, it usually costs about $550 a year.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Trace inside Conway city limits?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Myrtle Trace has a Conway mailing address but is outside the city, so owners there pay no Conway city tax.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://myrtletracesc.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Trace HOA</a>, <a href="https://myrtletracesc.org/wp-content/uploads/Guidelines/MyrtleTraceCovenant.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HOA rules</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County deed records</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=101%20Myrtle%20Trace%20Drive%2C%20Conway%2C%20SC%2029526" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood map</a>. Not legal or tax advice. The home sizes are from recent home listings. Drive times are OpenStreetMap estimates with no traffic. The flood cost is FEMA's middle policy price for this ZIP code.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Myrtle Trace from above, with the golf course next door. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew the outline from Horry County GIS parcels, added the labels and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Houses along two streets and a pond in Myrtle Trace, from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut a close view of one street from the aerial photo and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">The riverwalk in Conway. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waccamaw_River_Warehouse_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Main Street in Conway. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conway_Downtown_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Myrtle Trace from above, with the golf course next door","caption":"Myrtle Trace from above, with the golf course next door. The orange line is the edge of the n