rx="7" ry="2.4" fill="#1c2028" opacity=".18"/><path d="M0 0C-3-6-13-14-13-26a13 13 0 1 1 26 0c0 12-10 20-13 26z" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5"/><use href="#c3r-seasons-at-prince-creek--home" x="-8.5" y="-34.5" width="17" height="17" color="#ffffff"/></g><text class="h" x="15" y="-14.5"><tspan x="15">Seasons</tspan></text></g></g></g></svg><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.6rem">Map of where Seasons at Prince Creek West is, near Murrells Inlet, with drive times by car. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure><p class="c3-map-links" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;margin:.6rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:760px;font-size:.95rem"><span style="color:var(--brass-ink);display:inline-flex"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg></span><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=33.586369,-79.070940" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Seasons at Prince Creek West in Google Maps</a></p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Murrells Inlet is on a salt marsh, with fishing boats and marinas. The MarshWalk on the map is a boardwalk along the marsh.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="759" alt="White fishing boats tied up at a marina on calm water in Murrells Inlet, South Carolina" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pollinator. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Pollinator</a></span></div><figcaption>Fishing boats at a marina in Murrells Inlet.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-are-the-homes-like-in-seasons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The homes">What are the homes like in Seasons?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most homes in Seasons are on one level, with 3 bedrooms and about 1,700 to 2,500 square feet. They were built from 2006 to 2016, so every home here is a resale now.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes are on curving streets around ponds. More than half of the land is shared by the owners, with ponds and woods.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-ctop"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Seasons at Prince Creek West from above, with its long, narrow edge drawn in orange, curving streets of homes around ponds, woods on the east side, and the clubhouse and entrance marked" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Seasons at Prince Creek West from above. The orange line is the edge of the neighborhood.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-homes-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-homes-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-homes-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="One-story homes with gray and tan roofs and wide lawns around a pond and a curving street in Seasons at Prince Creek West, seen from above" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Homes around a pond in Seasons at Prince Creek West, from above.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="can-you-live-in-seasons-part-of-the-year"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Living here part-time">Can you live in Seasons part of the year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, as long as the person who is 55 or older lives in Seasons at least six months a year, under the <a href="https://www.seasons55.com/editor_upload/File/Community%20Management/Policies%20%26%20Rules/communitycharter2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">homeowners association (HOA) rules</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You cannot rent the home out for the months you are away. A lease here must be at least a year.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Read the Seasons age rules with an agent.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">An agent at Chapter3 can read the age and visitor rules with you before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Talk to an agent</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-does-it-cost-to-live-in-seasons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Costs">What does it cost to live in Seasons?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Seasons homes usually sell for about $500,000. The HOA fee is about $340 a month, and it includes internet, weekly trash pickup and lawn care.</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>One bill.</strong> The fees for the larger Prince Creek West area around Seasons come on your Seasons HOA bill, so there is no second bill.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>When you buy,</strong> you pay the HOA two months of dues, about $700, as a one-time fee. There is also a small transfer fee.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>Property tax.</strong> If you live in the home, the tax on a home at that price is about $2,000 a year. Seasons is outside any city limits, so there is no city tax.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">See <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how Horry County works out the tax on a home near Murrells Inlet</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the list of Seasons homes for sale.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us what you are looking for, and one of our agents will send you the homes for sale now.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-are-the-house-rules-in-seasons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="House rules">What are the house rules in Seasons?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Seasons, pets, fences, renting and golf carts are allowed, each with a rule.</p><ul role="list" style="list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(18rem,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px"><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 13c-2.5 0-5 2.6-5 5 0 1.6 1.2 2.5 2.6 2.5.9 0 1.6-.5 2.4-.5s1.5.5 2.4.5c1.4 0 2.6-.9 2.6-2.5 0-2.4-2.5-5-5-5z"/><circle cx="5.3" cy="11" r="1.8"/><circle cx="9" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="15" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="18.7" cy="11" r="1.8"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Pets</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Up to two. Keep them on a leash outside unless they are in a fenced yard.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Renting it out</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Yes, with a written lease of at least a year.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 21V4M20 21V4M3 4h2M19 4h2M4 8q8-3.5 16 0M8 6.9V21M12 6.3V21M16 6.9V21M4 17h16"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Fences</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Yes, once the neighborhood's design board approves it. It must line up with the sides of the house.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 4h12M6 4v8M14 4v8M5 17.5H3V12h12l3-4h1.5L21 13v4.5h-2M9 17.5h6"/><circle cx="7" cy="17.5" r="2"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="2"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Golf carts</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Park them in your garage, not on the street.</span></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-does-seasons-compare-with-other-55-neighborhoods"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Compare">How does Seasons compare with other 55+ neighborhoods?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Seasons usually sells for less than either Del Webb, and it is closer to the beach than Myrtle Trace.</p><style>.c3-cmp tr.c3-self td{background:#fff;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy)!important}@media (max-width:599px){.c3-cmp tr.c3-self{background:#fff;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cmp tr.c3-self td{background:transparent}}@media (max-width:599px){.c3-cmp table,.c3-cmp tbody,.c3-cmp tr,.c3-cmp td{display:block;width:100%}.c3-cmp thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)}.c3-cmp tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .75rem;padding:.4rem 0}.c3-cmp td{border:0!important;padding:.25rem .9rem!important}.c3-cmp td:first-child{color:var(--navy)!important;font-weight:500;font-size:1rem}.c3-cmp td[data-label]:not(:first-child)::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy)}.c3-cmp td a{padding:11px 0}}</style><div class="c3-cmp" style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Community</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Area</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Minutes to the beach by car</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">HOA fee a month</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Resale homes usually sell for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">North Myrtle Beach</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $315</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $535,000</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb at Grande Dunes</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $400 for a house</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $665,000 for a house</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/myrtle-trace/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Trace</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 15</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$95</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $300,000</td></tr><tr class="c3-self"><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:700">Seasons at Prince Creek West</strong></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Murrells Inlet</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $340</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $500,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1.2rem;margin:1.6rem 0 1.2rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass-ink);font-weight:600;margin:0 0 .4rem">From our files</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An agent at Chapter3 helped clients who owned a house in Blackmoor, a golf neighborhood in Murrells Inlet with no age rule. They sold that house and bought in Seasons, a few minutes away.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-are-the-pros-and-cons-of-living-in-seasons-at-prince"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Seasons at Prince Creek West has a gate, two pools and stores close by.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>There is a gate at the main entrance, with a call box for visitors.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Publix and the hospital are each less than 10 minutes away by car.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The Murrells Inlet MarshWalk is about 10 minutes away by car.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The beach is a drive, not a walk. The nearest beach access is in Garden City.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Golf carts must be parked in the garage, not on the street.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>On some lots, one corner touches the high-risk flood zone. <span class="c3-pc-do">An agent checks the flood map for the house you like before you offer.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="will-a-seasons-lot-need-flood-insurance"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood insurance">Will a Seasons lot need flood insurance?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most Seasons lots will not. On 45 of the lots, one corner touches the high-risk flood zone on <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=130%20Grand%20Cypress%20Way%2C%20Murrells%20Inlet%2C%20SC%2029576" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the federal flood map</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the house itself is in the zone, your lender will require flood insurance. Outside the zone, flood insurance is your choice. A policy here usually costs about $600 a year.</p><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> Carol and Jim are moving from Buffalo, and they want a house in Seasons that backs onto the woods. They find one they like and plan to make an offer that night.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">First, their Chapter3 agent checks the government's flood map for that house. The back of the house is in the high-risk flood area, so their lender will require flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">That is a yearly bill Carol and Jim had not planned on. The agent gets them a quote that afternoon, and they make their offer that night knowing the cost.</p></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get a flood insurance quote on the lot you like.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the home you are looking at. One of our agents can help you get a flood <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">insurance</a> quote on it before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get a flood quote</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="seasons-at-prince-creek-west-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Seasons at Prince Creek West FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Seasons at Prince Creek West a gated community?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. There is a gate at the main entrance, with a call box for visitors.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is the HOA fee in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA fee is about $340 a month. It includes internet, weekly trash pickup and lawn care.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are there new homes for sale in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The builder has finished, so every home for sale in Seasons is a resale.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can someone under 55 live in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, if a resident 55 or older also lives in the home. No one under 18 can live there.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How old are the homes in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes were built from 2006 to 2016. Most are on one level, with 3 bedrooms.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is Seasons at Prince Creek West from the beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 13 minutes by car without traffic, to the nearest public beach access with parking, in Garden City.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.seasons55.com/editor_upload/File/Community%20Management/Policies%20%26%20Rules/communitycharter2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HOA rules</a>, <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/care-compare/details/hospital/420098/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tidelands Waccamaw on Medicare Care Compare</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County deed records</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=130%20Grand%20Cypress%20Way%2C%20Murrells%20Inlet%2C%20SC%2029576" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood map</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Federal flood insurance law</a>. For education, not legal advice. The HOA fee, the gate and the home sizes are from recent home listings. Drive times are no-traffic estimates from OpenStreetMap. The flood cost is the middle FEMA policy price in ZIP code 29576.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The clubhouse from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew the outline from Horry County GIS parcels, added the labels and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Fishing boats at a marina in Murrells Inlet. Photo: Pollinator, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murrells_inlet2473.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Seasons at Prince Creek West from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew the outline from Horry County GIS parcels, added the labels and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Homes around a pond in Seasons at Prince Creek West, from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut a close view of one street from the aerial photo and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-clubhouse-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-clubhouse-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The clubhouse from abo