 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Myrtle Beach neighborhoods are closest to the beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Cherry Grove is closest, with a public beach access about a tenth of a mile from the middle of the neighborhood. On the ocean side of Surfside Beach, the sand is about a nine-minute walk. The Market Common is about five minutes from the beach by car."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Carolina Forest or Myrtle Beach better to live in?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The city of Myrtle Beach is better for being close to the beach, and Carolina Forest for big neighborhood pools and lakes. Plantation Lakes, Waterbridge, Avalon and The Farm, all in Carolina Forest, are 12 to 20 minutes from the beach by car."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which neighborhoods near Myrtle Beach have no HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most homes for sale on the ocean side of Surfside Beach, and more than half in Cherry Grove, are listed with no HOA fee. Most other neighborhoods on this page have an HOA fee of under $250 a month for a house."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there 55+ communities near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Del Webb North Myrtle Beach, Del Webb at Grande Dunes, Seasons at Prince Creek West and Myrtle Trace are 55+ communities, and our 55+ guide compares them."}}]}</script>
