 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach a buyer's market?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For condos, yes: across Horry County, the condos for sale would take about 7.5 months to sell. For houses under $700,000, not yet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will home prices in Myrtle Beach go down?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not forecast prices. Horry County house prices were about flat in the latest year, after four years of gains."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a lawyer to buy a house in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every South Carolina home closing must be supervised by a South Carolina attorney. Step 5 says how you choose one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a CL-100?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The termite letter, the Official South Carolina Wood Infestation Report. Only a licensed pest control applicator may issue it for a sale or a loan. It reports visible insect damage, active infestations, and moisture and decay under the house."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I rent my Myrtle Beach condo by the night?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, if it is inside the City of Myrtle Beach, where most condos sit in zones that allow it. The condo's own rules can still ban it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are property taxes in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, on a house the county values at $350,000, about $1,410 a year if you live in it and apply. As a second home, about $5,350."}}]}</script>
