+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a Horry County flood map PDF?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. FEMA's Flood Map Service Center lets you download or print the official flood map for any address in the county."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How new is Horry County's flood map?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The countywide map took effect in December 2021. FEMA has revised four small areas of it since, most recently in September 2026."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Zone X mean I do not need flood insurance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No federal rule makes you buy it in Zone X, but some lenders still ask. FEMA recommends flood insurance even where a lender does not require it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use private flood insurance for the loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if the policy meets the federal rule. Under federal law, a lender must accept private flood insurance that does. A private policy has its own wait before it starts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a cash buyer get the flood zone notice?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The written notice comes from a lender with the loan, so a cash buyer gets none."}}]}</script>
