 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a gate make a neighborhood safer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not rate any neighborhood as safe or unsafe. The price table shows which gates have a guard, a gatehouse, a keypad or a call box."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do guests get through the gate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"By a guard with a guest list, a call box at the gate, or a code from the owner. When you tour homes with us, we set up the visit with the gate before we go."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a gated community in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, not inside the town. Prestwick, about a mile outside it, is the gated neighborhood on this page nearest Surfside Beach."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there 55+ gated communities near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Seasons at Prince Creek West in Murrells Inlet is the 55+ community on this page, and visitors use a call box at its main entrance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there gated golf communities near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Most of the places on this page are golf communities, from Tidewater in North Myrtle Beach to DeBordieu Colony."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Barefoot Resort a gated community?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only in part. Barefoot Resort in North Myrtle Beach is mostly open, with a few gated neighborhoods inside it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Grande Dunes a gated community?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only in part. Grande Dunes in Myrtle Beach is a large planned community, and only some of its sections have gates."}}]}</script>
