 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach in a flood zone?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Parts of it are. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, only about 1 in 23 houses is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. About 1 in 4 condos in the city is."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you rent out a house near the beach in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The rules differ by city. In the City of Myrtle Beach, a rental of less than 90 days is legal only where the zoning allows it. About 96 in 100 houses there are not in those zones. North Myrtle Beach allows short-term rentals across the city, with a city business license renewed each year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a condo near the beach cheaper than a house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In North Myrtle Beach, yes. In its beach sections, a condo sold for about $310,000 to $360,000 at the middle in the last year. This page covers houses; our condos page covers condos."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a second-row house at the beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A second-row house is in the row just behind the oceanfront houses. Our waterfront homes page covers the oceanfront row itself."}}]}</script>
