+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you do a perc test before buying land in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"South Carolina has not used perc tests since the late 1970s. The state's septic permit takes their place: a $150 application with the deed or the lot's survey map, then a soil visit. We can write your offer so it depends on the lot passing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is the cheapest land for sale near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Around Loris, Green Sea and Nichols, where an acre is listed at about $25,000 on tracts of an acre or more. Around Aynor it is about $40,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you put a mobile home on land in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In the county's FA and CFA zones, yes, on a lot of at least half an acre. In the SF zones, no. Deed restrictions on the land can still bar one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there hunting land for sale in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. In our count, 30 Horry land listings are marked for hunting. Tell us the size and the area you want, and we send you the tracts that fit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does land cost around Pawleys Island?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In the Pawleys Island area, in Georgetown County, an acre is listed at about $342,000 on tracts of an acre or more. That is the highest of the areas we counted."}}]}</script>
