 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I find a new house in Myrtle Beach under $300,000?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. About 1 in 5 new houses for sale in Horry County is listed at $300,000 or less. Of the ten communities where builders sold the most, The Overlook (Indigo Grove), Kingston Oaks and Cypress Ridge had typical sale prices under $300,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there new townhomes in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. 108 new townhouses are for sale in Horry County, at a typical list price of about $275,000 for about 1,580 square feet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the county know a new house is being built?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"From the building permit. South Carolina law has every county require a permit for new construction. The county must send the assessor a copy of each building permit within 10 days, so the assessor knows a house is being built."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a home builder in South Carolina need a license?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A residential builder needs a state license for any job over $5,000, issued by the Residential Builders Commission. A complaint against a builder goes to the Commission in writing and sworn."}}]}</script>
