-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">New Construction</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Buying a new build on the Grand Strand</p><h1 class="detail-h1">New construction in Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">what the price on the sign leaves out.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">New construction in Horry County costs about what a nearly new house does. The sign leaves out lot premiums, options, HOA charges, closing costs and the full tax bill.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A new house here lists for about the same price per square foot as a house built 2016 to 2023 of similar size nearby. A typical new house for sale is listed at about $370,000. Most are built inland, in large communities near Highway 90, Highway 22 and the Carolina Bays Parkway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The sign leaves out the full tax bill, closing costs, HOA charges, options you pick and lot premiums, extra charges for a particular lot. For about 4 in 5 of the 2026 builder sales, the county still taxes only the lot. On a typical home you live in outside city limits, the yearly county bill goes fr