 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I park a boat at my house in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, on your own lot, within the rule of the town it is in; the table under What can you do at home gives each one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which areas near Myrtle Beach almost always have an HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Carolina Forest, the Grande Dunes, the Market Common and Burgess: almost every home for sale there has an HOA fee. Almost all homes for sale in Little River's named subdivisions have an HOA fee too. Longs and the country around Conway look rural, but most homes for sale there have an HOA fee too."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there homes with no HOA in Murrells Inlet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, but only a little more than 1 in 4 homes for sale with a Murrells Inlet address is listed with no HOA fee. At the north end of the inlet, by the creeks and the Stanley Drive landing, almost every house for sale has none."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there homes with no HOA in North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. More than half of the homes for sale with a North Myrtle Beach address are listed with no HOA fee. Almost all of them are in Cherry Grove, Crescent Beach, Windy Hill and Ocean Drive."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a typical HOA fee in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About $95 a month on a house. A condo fee is much higher because it includes the building's insurance, water and sewer, trash and a pool."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you buy a condo with no HOA fee in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Almost never. Of about 2,700 condos for sale around Myrtle Beach, only one was listed with no HOA fee. South Carolina law makes condo owners share the cost of the building."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a listing with no HOA fee mean the home has no HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not always. A blank fee means no fee was listed. We check the deed and the county records for an HOA before you make an offer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a campground home with no HOA fee a no-HOA home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. A campground home has no HOA fee, but it sits on leased land, and you pay a yearly lease for the land under it."}}]}</script>
