 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there homes with a pool under $300,000 in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Few. On the day we counted, 5 of the 575 houses for sale in Horry County at $300,000 or less had their own pool. 168 houses at that price were in a neighborhood with a shared pool."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a pool add value to a home in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On asking prices, yes. At every size we checked, houses with a pool ask more than houses without one. Part of that gap comes from where they are: nearer the beach and more often on the water."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do pool homes in Myrtle Beach allow short-term rentals?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"More often than other houses. About 28 percent of houses for sale with their own pool say short-term rentals are allowed, against about 12 percent of all houses."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are pool homes near Myrtle Beach in gated communities?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 1 in 5 houses for sale with their own pool is in a gated community, against about 1 in 9 of all houses."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do townhouses near Myrtle Beach have a pool?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many share one. Half of the 298 townhouses for sale in Horry County, 149, are in a community with a shared pool. Their middle asking price is about $270,000."}}]}</script>
