+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/property-records/">Property records</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">GIS Map</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County property records</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Horry County GIS map: find any parcel, its lines and its tax map number<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Every lot in the county, with its lines, its zoning and aerial photos back to 1998.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 14, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The county's parcel map now opens on a sign-in screen. Three steps get you from that screen to a lot's lines, acreage and zoning.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Horry County GIS map is the county's parcel map, and it now asks you to sign in with a county account before it shows the map. Once in, search by address, owner, PIN or TMS, then click the lot.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The card gives the owner, the PIN, the zoning, the acreage and the deed book and page. The lines on the map are drawn for taxes, not surveyed.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="steps"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;lin