+})();
+})();</script></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 14, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Type an address. The card shows Horry County's and FEMA's public records for it, line by line, with no sign-in.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County keeps property records in three places: deeds at the Register of Deeds, tax bills at the Treasurer, and lot lines on the county's online map (GIS).</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our free lookup reads the county's and FEMA's public maps for one address. Its card opens that parcel's deed record and tax bill.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="city-line"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Your mail says Myrtle Beach. The city line may not.</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 4 street addresses that say "Myrtle Beach" are outside the City of Myrtle Beach. The city in a mailing address comes from the post office, not from the town line. Across Horry County, about 7 in 10 street addresses are outside every city and town. We checked all 246,621 points on the county's address map against the town limits.</p><figure class="pr-chart"><p class="pr-chart-t">Most Myrtle Beach mailing addresses are outside the city</p><div class="pr-bars" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart. Share of street addresses with each mailing city that are outside that town's limits: Myrtle Beach 74%, Conway 73%, Surfside Beach 66%, North Myrtle Beach 4%."><div class="pr-bar"><div class="pr-bar-h"><span class="pr-bar-c">Myrtle Beach</span><span>74% outside</span></div><span class="pr-track"><i style="width:73.7%"></i></span></div><div class="pr-bar"><div class="pr-bar-h"><span class="pr-bar-c">Conway</span><span>73% outside</span></div><span class="pr-track"><i style="width:73.4%"></i></span></div><div class="pr-bar"><div class="pr-bar-h"><span class="pr-bar-c">Surfside Beach</span><span>66% outside</span></div><span class="pr-track"><i style="width:65.9%"></i></span></div><div class="pr-bar"><div class="pr-bar-h"><span class="pr-bar-c">North Myrtle Beach</span><span>4% outside</span></div><span class="pr-track"><i style="width:3.9%"></i></span></div></div><figcaption>Share of street addresses with each mailing city that are outside that town's limits, from Horry County's address map.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The line matters when you buy. Inside a town, the town's zoning applies. Outside, the county's does: see <a href="/buyers/property-records/gis-map/#zoning" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what the county's zoning codes mean</a>.</p><p class="pr-quiet">Not sure which side an address is on? <a href="#lookup" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Look it up</a>: the card's Town line says.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where records are">Where are Horry County property records kept?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each county office keeps its own records, and each has its own search.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What you want</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where Horry County keeps it</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Our guide</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The deed, a mortgage, a lien or a plat (a surveyor's drawing of the lots)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Where Horry County keeps it">The Register of Deeds. Its index is online; the documents are not.</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Our guide"><a href="/buyers/property-records/deeds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Horry County land records</a></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The lot lines, zoning code and aerial photos</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Where Horry County keeps it">The county's online map, after you sign in with a county account</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Our guide"><a href="/buyers/property-records/gis-map/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Horry County GIS map</a></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The tax bill, or paying it</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Where Horry County keeps it">The Treasurer's tax search, with no sign-in</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Our guide"><a href="/buyers/property-records/tax-bill/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Horry County tax bills</a></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The flood zone and what it means</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Where Horry County keeps it">FEMA's flood map. Our lookup reads it for any Horry County address.</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Our guide"><a href="/buyers/flood-zone-check/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Flood zone check</a></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">What the home would sell for</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Where Horry County keeps it">Not a county record</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Our guide"><a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What homes sold for, by area</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/hoa-liens-and-foreclosure/horry-government-justice-center-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/hoa-liens-and-foreclosure/horry-government-justice-center-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/hoa-liens-and-foreclosure/horry-government-justice-center-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="675" alt="The Horry County Government and Justice Center in Conway: brick wings on each side of a white columned entrance, seen across the parking lot" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pollinator at English Wikipedia. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Pollinator at English Wikipedia</a></span></div><figcaption>The Horry County Government and Justice Center at 1301 Second Avenue in Conway, where the Register of Deeds' public viewing area is.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Looking for the property appraiser? Horry County calls that office the Assessor. The Assessor values property, the Auditor bills the tax and the Treasurer collects it.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Skip the three county websites.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Comparing a few homes? An agent gathers the county records for each one and tells you what stands out, free.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Let us make it simple</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="by-name"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Search by name">Can you search Horry County property records by name?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, in two county searches. Both ask for the last name first.</p><ul class="pr-list"><li><strong>The deed index at the Register of Deeds.</strong> It is free and needs no account. Our <a href="/buyers/property-records/deeds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">deed search guide</a> shows the steps.</li><li><strong>The Treasurer's tax search.</strong> It also finds a bill by parcel number or notice number. Our <a href="/buyers/property-records/tax-bill/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">tax bill guide</a> shows the steps.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county's map searches by owner too, after you sign in with a county account. Our lookup works by address only and shows no names.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="not-shown"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What records leave out">What do Horry County property records not show?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Four things a buyer needs to know are not in the deed index, the tax bill or the county map.</p><ul class="pr-list"><li><strong>Unpaid HOA charges.</strong> A condo buyer and the seller can both owe the seller's unpaid HOA charges, up to the amount in the statement the association must give on request. Our agents check the balance before closing, and an unpaid fee is usually paid from the seller's proceeds. See <a href="/hoa/estoppel-and-transfer-fees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA statements and transfer fees</a>.</li><li><strong>Rental rules.</strong> Whether a home can be rented by the night depends on the town and the HOA, not on the deed or the tax bill. See <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the Myrtle Beach short-term rental rules</a> and <a href="/hoa/rental-restrictions/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA rental restrictions</a>.</li><li><strong>The cost of insurance.</strong> It is not a county record. See <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what coastal home insurance costs</a>.</li><li><strong>Your own tax bill.</strong> Last year's bill can be the seller's, figured at the 4% ratio. Yours is figured at 4% if it is your legal residence, which you apply for, and at 6% if not. See <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Horry County property taxes</a>.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have us check what the records leave out.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Before you make an offer, we check the HOA balance, the rental rules and the tax for that home, free.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check the home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="georgetown"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Georgetown County">Pawleys Island and Litchfield: Georgetown County records</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pawleys Island and Litchfield Beach are in Georgetown County, so their records are Georgetown's. Our lookup reads Horry County's maps only.</p><ul class="pr-list"><li><strong>The map:</strong> Georgetown's <a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/fa729743d97047579f348d68f9643ba1" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">online map</a> opens with no sign-in. It searches by tax map number, address or road, not by owner.</li><li><strong>Deeds:</strong> <a href="https://www.georgetowndeeds.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">georgetowndeeds.com</a> shows document images online when it has them.</li><li><strong>Tax bills:</strong> <a href="https://georgetowncountysctax.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">georgetowncountysctax.com</a>.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pawleys Island</a> itself is less than 4 miles long and mostly one house wide, with a salt marsh between it and the mainland. The island and most of the land around it share ZIP code 29585, so a Pawleys Island address does not always mean a house on the island.</p><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="city=Pawleys+Island&amp;type=house" data-head="Houses for sale in Pawleys Island"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="horry-county-property-records-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Horry County property records questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How do I find the owner of a property in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Look up the address, then tap Deed record on the card. The county's deed record names the parties to that deed. The Treasurer's tax search, behind the Tax bill button, also shows the owner's name.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why can't the lookup find my address?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Type the house number and the street, then pick a suggestion. Without a house number, the county's address finder can match only the street, so the card cannot name a parcel.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why does a condo building show many parcel numbers?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each unit in the building has its own parcel number, drawn on the building's outline. Send us the unit number and we find the right one.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is my hurricane evacuation zone?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Type the address in the lookup. The card's Hurricane line gives zone A, B or C, or none. About 1 in 3 street addresses in Horry County is in a zone.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who answers flood map questions in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Code Enforcement has 12 certified floodplain managers on staff. To reach one, call its flood office at (843) 915-5090.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://gisportal.horrycounty.org/server/rest/services/Locators/County_Locator/GeocodeServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County address finder</a>, <a href="https://gisportal.horrycounty.org/server/rest/services/OpenData" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County open data</a>, <a href="https://hazards.fema.gov/arcgis/rest/services/public/NFHL/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood hazard layer</a>, <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-44/section-64.3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">44 CFR 64.3</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 U.S.C. 4012a</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kw5fxufi/flood-news-flyer-with-ppa-feb-2026.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Flood News</a>, <a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/fa729743d97047579f348d68f9643ba1" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown County map</a>. Our counts: all 246,621 points on Horry County's address map, placed inside or outside each town's limits and evacuation zone. One point is one street address; a condo building can be one point. Not legal advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The Horry County Government and Justice Center at 1301 Second Avenue in Conway, where the Register of Deeds' public viewing area is. Photo: Pollinator at English Wikipedia, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Horry_County_Courthouse_and_county_office_complex,_Conway,_South_Carolina_(18_November_2006).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/hoa-liens-and-foreclosure/horry-government-justice-center-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/hoa-liens-and-foreclosure/horry-government-justice-center-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The Horry County Government and Justice Center at 1301 Second Avenue in Conway, where the Register of Deeds' public viewing area is","caption":"The Horry County Government and Justice Center at 1301 Second Avenue in Conway, where the Register of Deeds' public viewing area is.","description":"The Horry County Government and Justice Center in Conway: brick wings on each side of a white columned entrance, seen across the parking lot","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Pollinator at English Wikipedia"},"creditText":"Pollinator at English Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© Pollinator at English Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 3.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Horry_County_Courthouse_and_county_office_complex,_Conway,_South_Carolina_(18_November_2006).jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Horry_County_Courthouse_and_county_office_complex,_Conway,_South_Carolina_(18_November_2006).jpg","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Horry County Government and Justice Center, 1301 Second Avenue, Conway, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Found a home you like? See it with a local agent.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">We set up the showing, walk the lot with you and answer what its records cannot.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Set up a showing</a></div></section></main>
