+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I pay Horry County taxes by phone?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, for a small fee, shown in the fee table above. For a question about a bill, the Treasurer's main line is (843) 915-5470."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get a copy of my Horry County tax receipt?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Print it from the Tax Payments and Receipts site: search the bill, then open it. A printed copy will not do for a car's first registration."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"I never got a tax bill. Am I still late?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The 3% penalty starts January 16 whether or not a bill arrived. The one exception is a home bought that year whose bill went to the seller."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a Horry County tax penalty be waived?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, in two cases. One is a home bought this year whose bill went to the seller. The other is a written request with clear proof you mailed the payment on time; the Treasurer's answer to it is final."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there unclaimed tax money in my name?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The county keeps a search of unclaimed tax refunds, by name or notice number, on its Tax Payer Services page. A claim takes 3 to 6 weeks. Refunds dated before 2022 are with the State Treasurer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is the Horry County tax office in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At 332 Hinson Drive in Carolina Forest, inside the county's Central Coast Complex."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Chapter3 part of Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Chapter3 is a real estate brokerage. The tax site, the bill and the payment belong to the Horry County Treasurer. We find a bill or pull it for buyers and owners, free."}}]}</script>
