 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-new-jersey/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much lower are property taxes in Myrtle Beach than New Jersey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Bergen County averages about 1.89 percent effective; Horry County averages about 0.38 percent on a primary home, and the primary rate removes the school operating tax. At published rates a $400,000 primary home in the unincorporated county bills roughly $1,470 a year. Seniors should first net off New Jersey's relief programs, which do not travel."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a New Jersey exit tax when you sell your house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It is an estimated tax withheld at closing when the seller is already a non-resident: the gain at the top rate, and never less than 2 percent of the sale price. It is reconciled on the New Jersey non-resident return and refunded to the extent it exceeds the actual tax. Raise the timing with your New Jersey closing attorney early."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will South Carolina tax my pension more than New Jersey does?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can. New Jersey excludes up to $100,000 of retirement income for a couple at 62 and older when total income is $150,000 or less, which beats South Carolina's deductions. Above that cliff New Jersey gives nothing and South Carolina's deductions win. Social Security is untaxed in both."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do Stay NJ, the Senior Freeze or ANCHOR transfer to South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. They are New Jersey programs and they end with the move. South Carolina's senior break is different: at 65, after one year of residency, the first $50,000 of a primary home's value is exempt, with no income test."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is the car tax in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is yearly: about $360 to $460 on a $30,000 car depending on the town, plus a $50 road fee, billed by the county before the plate will renew. Each vehicle also pays a one-time $250 fee at its first South Carolina registration, within 45 days of the move."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What gets more expensive after leaving New Jersey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Clothing gains an 8 to 9 percent sales tax, every vehicle picks up the yearly tax, and coastal insurance is usually higher than an inland New Jersey policy. Price an insurance quote early; it is the line that moves a monthly budget most."}}]}</script>
