flights and its history.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">If you want</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Choose</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">More home for the same money</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">The typical home costs about a fifth less.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A lower yearly property tax</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">The middle bill is about $750 a year less.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The beach on a weeknight</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">The city is on the ocean. Charleston's beaches are on islands, in towns of their own.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A newer house</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">Half the homes were built in 2003 or later.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A shorter drive to work</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">About 25 minutes on average, against about 30.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A local job in a big market</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">More than twice as many working residents, and higher pay.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">More flights</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">Its airport boards about 1.8 times as many passengers.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A teaching hospital nearby</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">MUSC, the state's only comprehensive academic health system, is there.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">History at your door</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">Fort Sumter and Fort Moultrie, run by the National Park Service.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Fewer freezing nights</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Choose">Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Why">About 6 a year downtown, against about 34 at the North Myrtle Beach airport.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our guide to <a href="/buyers/relocating/getting-around/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">getting around Myrtle Beach</a> has the drive to Charleston, the roads and the airport.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="home-prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">Is it cheaper to live in Myrtle Beach than Charleston?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. The typical home in the Myrtle Beach area is worth about $340,000, and in the Charleston area about $437,000. That is about $98,000 less.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Census Bureau's survey of homeowners shows about the same difference: about $105,000 between the two areas' middle home values. In the past year, values held about flat in both areas.</p><figure class="c3-gchart"><span class="cap">The difference in typical home value has almost doubled in ten years</span><ul class="mbc-key" aria-hidden="true"><li><i style="background:#2a3040"></i>Charleston area</li><li><i style="background:#c4783a"></i>Myrtle Beach area</li></ul><svg class="mbc-n" viewBox="0 0 280 252" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the typical home value each September from 2016 to 2026. The Charleston area rose from about $241,000 to about $437,000, and the Myrtle Beach area from about $189,000 to about $340,000. The difference grew from about $52,500 to about $98,000."><line x1="56" x2="270" y1="195.5" y2="195.5" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="50" y="200.4" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">$200K</text><line x1="56" x2="270" y1="131.4" y2="131.4" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="50" y="136.3" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">$300K</text><line x1="56" x2="270" y1="67.3" y2="67.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="50" y="72.2" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">$400K</text><text x="56.0" y="245.0" text-anchor="start" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">2016</text><text x="163.0" y="245.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">2021</text><text x="270.0" y="245.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">2026</text><path d="M56.0 169.1L77.4 159.3L98.8 150.7L120.2 145.7L141.6 137.2L163.0 101.9L184.4 60.1L205.8 52.6L227.2 40.8L248.6 42.6L270.0 43.3" fill="none" stroke="#2a3040" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M56.0 202.8L77.4 197.3L98.8 190.2L120.2 183.3L141.6 175.7L163.0 144.8L184.4 103.0L205.8 101.3L227.2 100.7L248.6 107.2L270.0 105.9" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="59.0" x2="59.0" y1="169.1" y2="202.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><text x="66.0" y="190.9" text-anchor="start" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$52,500 apart</text><line x1="267.0" x2="267.0" y1="43.3" y2="105.9" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><text x="260.0" y="79.5" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$98K apart</text><circle cx="270.0" cy="43.3" r="4.5" fill="#2a3040"/><circle cx="270.0" cy="105.9" r="4.5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="270" y="32.1" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#2a3040" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$437,000</text><text x="270" y="126.9" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$340,000</text></svg><svg class="mbc-w" viewBox="0 0 660 330" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the typical home value each September from 2016 to 2026. The Charleston area rose from about $241,000 to about $437,000, and the Myrtle Beach area from about $189,000 to about $340,000. The difference grew from about $52,500 to about $98,000."><line x1="52" x2="650" y1="265.2" y2="265.2" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="46" y="269.7" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">$200K</text><line x1="52" x2="650" y1="174.7" y2="174.7" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="46" y="179.2" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">$300K</text><line x1="52" x2="650" y1="84.2" y2="84.2" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="46" y="88.7" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">$400K</text><text x="52.0" y="323.5" text-anchor="start" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">2016</text><text x="171.6" y="323.5" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">2018</text><text x="291.2" y="323.5" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">2020</text><text x="410.8" y="323.5" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">2022</text><text x="530.4" y="323.5" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">2024</text><text x="650.0" y="323.5" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">2026</text><path d="M52.0 227.9L111.8 214.0L171.6 201.9L231.4 194.9L291.2 182.9L351.0 133.0L410.8 74.0L470.6 63.4L530.4 46.8L590.2 49.3L650.0 50.2" fill="none" stroke="#2a3040" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M52.0 275.4L111.8 267.7L171.6 257.7L231.4 247.9L291.2 237.2L351.0 193.6L410.8 134.6L470.6 132.1L530.4 131.3L590.2 140.5L650.0 138.7" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="55.0" x2="55.0" y1="227.9" y2="275.4" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><text x="62.0" y="256.2" text-anchor="start" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$52,500 apart</text><line x1="647.0" x2="647.0" y1="50.2" y2="138.7" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><text x="640.0" y="99.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$98,000 apart</text><circle cx="650.0" cy="50.2" r="4.5" fill="#2a3040"/><circle cx="650.0" cy="138.7" r="4.5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="650" y="39.8" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#2a3040" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$437,000</text><text x="650" y="158.2" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$340,000</text></svg><figcaption>Zillow's typical home value for all homes, each September. Both areas rose about 80% since 2016, so the difference in dollars almost doubled.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Everyday prices are lower too. On the federal government's price index, prices in the Myrtle Beach area are about 7% lower overall. To compare your own budget, use our <a href="/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">cost of living calculator</a>.</p><style>main#main .hx-qs{margin:1rem 0 1.4rem}main#main .hx-strip.hx-qs:empty{display:block!important;height:0;margin:0;overflow:hidden}</style><script>(function(){function fill(s){if(s.getAttribute("data-done"))return;s.setAttribute("data-done","1");fetch("/homes/api/strip?"+s.getAttribute("data-q"),{credentials:"same-origin"}).then(function(r){return r.ok?r.json():null}).then(function(j){if(!j||!j.ok||!j.html||j.html.indexOf("hx-s-empty")>-1)return;var hd=document.createElement("p");hd.className="hx-s-head";var b=document.createElement("b");b.textContent=s.getAttribute("data-head");hd.appendChild(b);if(j.link&&j.link.charAt(0)==="/"){var a=document.createElement("a");a.href=j.link;a.textContent="See all";hd.appendChild(a)}var row=document.createElement("div");row.className="hx-s-row";row.innerHTML=j.html;s.appendChild(hd);s.appendChild(row);if(j.note){var n=document.createElement("p");n.className="hx-s-note";n.textContent=j.note;s.insertBefore(n,row)}}).catch(function(){})}function go(){var all=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll(".hx-qs[data-q]"));if(!("IntersectionObserver" in window)){all.forEach(fill);return}var io=new IntersectionObserver(function(es){es.forEach(function(e){if(e.isIntersecting){io.unobserve(e.target);fill(e.target)}})},{rootMargin:"600px 0px"});all.forEach(function(s){io.observe(s)})}if(document.readyState==="loading")document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",go);else go()})();</script><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;max=437000" data-head="A whole house here for less than Charleston's typical home"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="the-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The beach">Which has more beach, Myrtle Beach or Charleston?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach is on the ocean. Downtown has a boardwalk about 1.3 miles long, beside the sand. After the summer season and until May 1, you can walk a leashed dog or ride a bike on the beach and the Boardwalk at any hour.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County has more than 360 public beach accesses, and Charleston County has 136. North Myrtle Beach alone has 167, more than Charleston County's whole coast. Parking and tent rules differ by town; our <a href="/buyers/relocating/beaches/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">beach rules by town</a> lists them.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Older two-story houses on lawns along the beach at left, and two tall condo towers on the beach at right, with streets of houses under oak trees behind, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses and condo towers on the beach in Myrtle Beach, with wooden walkways over the dunes to the sand.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Charleston's beaches are on its islands. From Charleston City Hall, Sullivan's Island and Folly Beach are each about 20 minutes by car with no traffic. On Sullivan's Island is Fort Moultrie, where patriots in a fort of palmetto logs beat the Royal Navy in 1776.</p><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="has=walk_to_beach&amp;type=house&amp;max=437000" data-head="Walk to the beach for less than Charleston's typical home"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="weather"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Weather">Is Myrtle Beach hotter than Charleston?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Near the ocean, no. Myrtle Beach and Charleston have about the same summer, with about three weeks a year at 90 degrees or more.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Days a year at 90 degrees or more: about the same near the ocean"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Days a year at 90 degrees or more: about the same near the ocean</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Weather station, where</span><span role="columnheader">Days a year at 90 degrees or more</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach airport</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">near the ocean</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.325" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">21 days</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Downtown Charleston</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">harbor station</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.381" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">25 days</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Charleston airport</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">inland, in North Charleston</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">64 days</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>NOAA's 1991 to 2020 averages at each weather station. Charleston's airport is inland, so it is hotter than either beach town.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Winter is colder here. The North Myrtle Beach airport has about 34 nights a year at or below freezing, and downtown Charleston about 6. Rain is about the same in both.</p><p class="mbc-story">One of our team found the first summer here hot and humid, got used to it within a short time, and now likes being outside.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Month by month, see <a href="/buyers/relocating/weather/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach weather</a>, with the ocean temperature.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="property-tax"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Property tax">Are property taxes lower in Myrtle Beach than Charleston?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. The middle property tax a homeowner pays is about $1,180 a year in the Myrtle Beach area and about $1,930 in the Charleston area.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The state's rule is the same in both: the home you live in is taxed on 4% of its fair market value, once you apply for it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The bills differ because each county, city and school district has its own tax rate. In Charleston County alone, the middle bill is about $2,310.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Horry County property tax guide</a> shows how to apply for the 4% rate, with a calculator.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the yearly tax on one house?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We work out its yearly property tax before you make an offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work out the tax on a home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flood"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood insurance">Is flood insurance more common in Charleston?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. FEMA estimates about one in seven residential buildings in Horry County are covered by a federal flood policy. In Charleston County, it is about one in three.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">FEMA also counts about three in ten residential buildings in Charleston County in its high-risk flood zone. Its file has no matching count for Horry County.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a house here, our agents check its flood zone and flood history before you make an offer. Our guides to <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">home, wind and flood insurance</a> and <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">finding out if a house has flooded</a> cover both.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Found a house you like?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We check its flood zone and any record of flooding before you make an offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a house's flood history</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="new-homes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="New homes">More new homes are being built in Myrtle Beach</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Half of all homes in the Myrtle Beach area, vacation homes included, were built in 2003 or later. In the Charleston area, the middle year is 1999.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In 2025, builders in the Myrtle Beach area took out permits for 6,418 new single-family houses. That is more than the Charleston area's 5,799, with less than half the people.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The construction cost on those permits, without the land, averaged about $218,000 here and at least $370,000 in the Charleston area. Our <a href="/buyers/new-construction/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">new construction guide</a> covers buying a new home here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="jobs"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Jobs and the commute">Charleston has more jobs and higher pay</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Charleston area has about 449,000 working residents, and the Myrtle Beach area about 185,000. The middle household income is about $93,000 there and about $71,000 here.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pay is higher there, and homes cost more by about the same share. In both areas, the middle home value is about 4.6 times the middle household income.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where people work</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Health care and education employ the most people in both. Here, about one in seven workers is in hotels, restaurants, entertainment and recreation. In the Charleston area, about one in ten works in manufacturing.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The drive to work</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The drive to work is shorter here: about 25 minutes on average, against about 30. About one in eight commuters here take 45 minutes or more, and about one in five in the Charleston area.</p><p class="mbc-story">In our experience, rush hour here adds 5 to 10 minutes, and leaving for work between 5 and 8 in the morning has few stops.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Who hires here, and what the work pays, is in our <a href="/buyers/relocating/jobs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">jobs guide</a>. Why so many people move here is in <a href="/buyers/relocating/why-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">why everyone is moving to Myrtle Beach</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="charleston"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What Charleston does better">What Charleston does better</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">More flights</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Charleston's airport is busier. About 3.1 million passengers boarded there in 2025, against about 1.7 million at Myrtle Beach International.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The state's teaching hospital</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Medical University of South Carolina, MUSC, is in Charleston. It is the state's only comprehensive academic health system, and its cancer center is the only one in the state the National Cancer Institute has designated.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For veterans, the <a href="https://www.va.gov/charleston-health-care/locations/myrtle-beach-va-clinic/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach VA Clinic</a> is an outpatient clinic in the VA Charleston system. That system's medical center, the Ralph H. Johnson VA Medical Center, is in Charleston. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/healthcare/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach hospitals guide</a> lists every hospital that serves the Grand Strand.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">History in the harbor</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two forts stand at the entrance to Charleston's harbor. Ferries leave downtown for Fort Sumter, where the Civil War began in April 1861.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For the full list of what is good and hard about living here, read <a href="/buyers/relocating/pros-and-cons/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">living in Myrtle Beach year-round</a>. Choosing a town on the Grand Strand next? Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">13 towns compared</a> puts each one side by side.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="myrtle-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What Myrtle Beach does better">What Myrtle Beach does better</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Charleston has real strengths, and Myrtle Beach has its own. These are the places Myrtle Beach comes out ahead.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Housing costs less in every way we measured</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The typical home is worth about $340,000, against about $437,000. Median rent is about $1,441 a month, against about $1,855. The middle property tax bill is about $1,180 a year, against about $1,930.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Far more new houses</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The 2025 permits work out to about 15 new single-family houses per 1,000 residents in the Myrtle Beach area. The Charleston area's figure is about 6.5.</p><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;max=437000&amp;yearMin=2024&amp;city=Myrtle+Beach" data-head="Myrtle Beach houses built since 2024, under Charleston's typical price"></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A beach that is the city itself</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach has 143 public beach accesses inside the city, and a boardwalk about 1.3 miles long. From Charleston City Hall, the nearest beach is about 20 minutes away by car.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A shorter drive to work</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The average one-way commute is about 25 minutes here, against about 30. About 1 in 8 commuters here drives 45 minutes or more, against about 1 in 5 in the Charleston area.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If these matter most to you, the houses above are where to start. A day of showings shows you the rest.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="myrtle-beach-vs-charleston-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Myrtle Beach vs Charleston FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Beach part of Charleston?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Myrtle Beach is in Horry County, and Charleston is in Charleston County. They are separate cities with separate local governments.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is Myrtle Beach from Charleston?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 98 miles by road, city hall to city hall. With no traffic, the drive takes about 2 hours 15 minutes each way.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which is bigger, Myrtle Beach or Charleston?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Charleston. The Charleston area has about 889,000 people, about twice the Myrtle Beach area's 428,000.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Charleston's airport bigger than Myrtle Beach's?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. The FAA ranks Charleston International a medium hub and Myrtle Beach International a small hub, by passengers boarded.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2025.B25077?g=310XX00US34820,16700" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census home values</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2025.B25103?g=310XX00US34820,16700" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census tax paid</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDP1Y2025.DP03?g=310XX00US34820,16700" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census jobs</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSST1Y2025.S0801?g=310XX00US34820,16700" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census commute</a>, <a href="https://www.bea.gov/data/prices-inflation/regional-price-parities-state-and-metro-area" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BEA prices</a>, <a href="https://gis.des.sc.gov/beachaccess/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.C. Beach Guide</a>, <a href="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/us-climate-normals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA normals</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/nfip-residential-penetration-rates-v1" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood policies</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/construction/bps/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census permits</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/charleston-health-care/locations/myrtle-beach-va-clinic/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA clinic</a>, <a href="https://www.faa.gov/airports/planning_capacity/passenger_allcargo_stats/passenger" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAA</a>, <a href="https://web.musc.edu/about" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MUSC</a>, <a href="https://www.nps.gov/fosu/index.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NPS</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R2685.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City of Myrtle Beach</a>. Areas are Census metro areas (Myrtle Beach: Horry County; Charleston: Berkeley, Charleston and Dorchester counties). Zillow: September value, all homes. Census values: owners' estimates. Flood: federal policies only. Permits: Census estimates, construction cost only. Not tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Houses and condo towers on the beach in Myrtle Beach, with wooden walkways over the dunes to the sand. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Plan a day of showings in Myrtle Beach.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Tell us your budget and what you want near you. We pick the homes with you and book the showings for one day.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Plan my showing day</a></div></section></main>
