-<div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/relocating/">Relocating</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Schools</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Zones, choice programs, and registration</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Schools, for buyers moving<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">to the Grand Strand.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated September 7, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">How Horry County school attendance zones are set and changed, the choice and charter options, the application-based academies, and when you qualify for in-state tuition, for buyers moving here.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem;display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#lead-form">Ask about a specific address</a><a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div>
+<div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/relocating/">Relocating</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Schools</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Zones, choice programs, and registration</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Schools, for buyers moving<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">to the Grand Strand.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 21, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">How Horry County school attendance zones are set and changed, the choice and charter options, the application-based academies, and when you qualify for in-state tuition, for buyers moving here.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem;display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#lead-form">Ask about a specific address</a><a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div>
 
 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The direct answer</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">How school zones work here</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools serves all of Horry County: Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, Conway, Carolina Forest, Socastee, Surfside Beach, Little River, Aynor, Loris, and the Horry side of Murrells Inlet. Georgetown County School District serves Pawleys Island, Litchfield, and the Georgetown side of Murrells Inlet. Every address is assigned one elementary, one middle, and one high school.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">Horry County publishes an address lookup tool. Georgetown County does not, so you call the district. Both change zones when schools open or fill, so confirm the assignment for the exact address before you write an offer that depends on it.</p></div></section>
 
