+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Medicare pay for assisted living in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Medicare and Medigap do not pay for long-term care, in a nursing home or in the community. Medicaid can, for those who qualify."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there help paying for assisted living in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, for some people. A state program called Optional State Supplementation helps pay for a licensed assisted living home enrolled in it, for a person with an approved slot. It is for people 65 or older, blind or disabled, under its income and savings limits. It is not Medicaid."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do assisted living homes near Myrtle Beach have a hurricane plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Each licensed assisted living home must have a written evacuation plan, made with the county's emergency agency and updated every year. A resident or the resident's responsible party can ask to read it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is independent living licensed in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. South Carolina licenses assisted living and nursing homes, but it has no license for independent living with no care."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does adult day care cost in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About $72 a day at the middle, or about $1,560 a month at five days a week. Horry County has 3 licensed adult day care centers, in Myrtle Beach, Conway and Loris."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is memory care in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There is no published local figure: the cost survey does not price memory care on its own. Prices differ from one home to the next."}}]}</script>
