em}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a month of care costs around Myrtle Beach"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a month of care costs around Myrtle Beach</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Kind of care</span><span role="columnheader">A month</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Adult day care, 5 days a week</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.158" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,560</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Assisted living</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.592" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$5,850</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Care at home, 44 hours a week</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.598" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$5,911</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Nursing home, shared room</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.9" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$8,900</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Nursing home, private room</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$9,900</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Middle monthly cost in the Myrtle Beach area, from CareScout's 2025 Cost of Care Survey. Care at home is a non-medical caregiver for 44 hours a week.</figcaption></figure><ul class="sl-list"><li><strong>Against the state and the country.</strong> Assisted living here costs more than South Carolina's $5,350 a month, and less than the U.S. figure of $6,200.</li><li><strong>Against other South Carolina areas.</strong> Of the areas the survey prices, Myrtle Beach is third highest, after Columbia and Hilton Head Island.</li><li><strong>Care at home.</strong> A non-medical caregiver, such as a home health aide or a homemaker, costs about $31 an hour. Adult day care costs about $72 a day.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The survey has no separate figure for memory care, and none for independent living. Prices differ from one home to the next, so we get each home's current prices for you.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Weigh a year of care against the house</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address of the house. An agent prices it from recorded sales nearby, so you can see how many years of care it would cover.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price the house</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="choices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The choices">Assisted living vs. nursing home vs. independent living: what is the difference?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each choice gives a different amount of care. In South Carolina, assisted living is licensed as a "community residential care facility", and the state's papers use both names.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table class="sl-choices" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Choice</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What you get</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Cost a month here</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">When more care is needed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Your own home, with help</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="What you get">Your house or condo, and a caregiver who comes in by the hour.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" class="num" data-l="Cost a month here">$31 an hour</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="When more care is needed">Add hours, or move to a place that gives care.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Independent living</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="What you get">An apartment or a home with no care included. The state has no license for it.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Cost a month here">No published local figure</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="When more care is needed">Hire help at home, or move to assisted living.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Assisted living</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="What you get">A room, at least three meals a day, and help with dressing, walking, bathing and taking medicines.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" class="num" data-l="Cost a month here">$5,850</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="When more care is needed">A nurse may come for up to 14 days in a row. Past that, a move.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Memory care</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="What you get">Alzheimer's care, often in its own unit of an assisted living home.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Cost a month here">No published local figure</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="When more care is needed">The same limits as assisted living.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Nursing home</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="What you get">An organized nursing staff that gives nursing care.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" class="num" data-l="Cost a month here">$8,900 shared, $9,900 private</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="When more care is needed">The level of care assisted living may not give.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Continuing care</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="What you get">One contract: an apartment or a cottage, and access to more care as needs change.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="Cost a month here">An entrance fee; each campus has its own</td><td style="padding:.6rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)" data-l="When more care is needed">More care, under the same contract.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Assisted living may not admit or keep a person who needs nursing home care or a nurse's daily attention. When the home's care, even with outside home health or hospice care, no longer meets a person's needs, the person must move within 30 days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina's health facility licensing law has no license for independent living. A home with room, board and personal help must be licensed as residential care.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Apartments with HUD rent help</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HUD pays subsidies to the owners of some apartment buildings to keep rents affordable for people with low incomes, including older adults. They are rental apartments, and none is on the state's list of licensed care homes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Horry County, HUD lists four of these buildings for older adults, with 228 apartments; one, with 110, is partly for people with disabilities. Two are in Myrtle Beach, one in Conway and one in Loris. One more is in Pawleys Island, with 48.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://resources.hud.gov/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD's Resource Locator</a> shows each building on a map. Ask the building's office about openings and who may rent there.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="by-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="By town">Where is assisted living around Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The state licenses 23 assisted living homes with 1,860 beds in Horry County and the Georgetown County side of Murrells Inlet and Pawleys Island. Each home is listed under the town in its mailing address, A to Z, with the beds the state licenses.</p><div class="sl-town"><h3>Myrtle Beach<span>8 homes, 718 beds</span></h3><p>Myrtle Beach addresses take in Carolina Forest, Grande Dunes and Socastee. Brightwater, a continuing care campus, is here.</p><p class="sl-hosp"><strong>Nearest main hospital, for most houses:</strong> Grand Strand Medical Center, about 12 minutes</p><ul class="sl-homes"><li>American House Myrtle Beach at Grande Dunes <span>122 beds</span></li><li>Arbor Landing at Surfside <span>40 beds</span></li><li>Brightwater Assisted Living <span>56 beds</span></li><li>Indigo at Carolina Forest <span>85 beds</span></li><li>Myrtle Beach Grove Senior Living <span>142 beds</span></li><li>Myrtle Beach Manor Retirement Community <span>111 beds</span></li><li>Portside at Grande Dunes <span>120 beds</span></li><li>Reflections at Carolina Forest <span>42 beds</span></li></ul><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;has=one_level&amp;city=Myrtle+Beach" data-head="One-level houses in Myrtle Beach, every room on one floor"></div></div><div class="sl-town"><h3>Murrells Inlet<span>5 homes, 455 beds</span></h3><p>Murrells Inlet addresses take in Garden City. Inlet Coastal Resort is on the Georgetown County side.</p><p class="sl-hosp"><strong>Nearest main hospital:</strong> Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital, about 6 minutes</p><ul class="sl-homes"><li>Inlet Coastal Resort <span>62 beds</span></li><li>Magnolia Bridge at Murrells Inlet <span>82 beds</span></li><li>Palmettos of Garden City <span>90 beds</span></li><li>Seabrook at Murrells Inlet <span>110 beds</span></li><li>Windrush at Garden City <span>111 beds</span></li></ul><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;has=one_level&amp;city=Murrells+Inlet" data-head="One-level houses in Murrells Inlet, every room on one floor"></div></div><div class="sl-town"><h3>Conway<span>5 homes, 248 beds</span></h3><p>Inland, about 29 minutes by car from the beach.</p><p class="sl-hosp"><strong>Nearest main hospital:</strong> Conway Medical Center, about 13 minutes</p><ul class="sl-homes"><li>Anderson Oaks Assisted Living <span>80 beds</span></li><li>Brookdale Conway <span>52 beds</span></li><li>Ladies Community Residence <span>8 beds</span></li><li>Lois Eargle Home <span>8 beds</span></li><li>Spring Oak Conway <span>100 beds</span></li></ul><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;has=one_level&amp;city=Conway" data-head="One-level houses in Conway, every room on one floor"></div></div><div class="sl-town"><h3>Little River<span>3 homes, 260 beds</span></h3><p>Just north of North Myrtle Beach.</p><p class="sl-hosp"><strong>Nearest main hospital:</strong> McLeod Health Seacoast, about 7 minutes</p><ul class="sl-homes"><li>Barclay at Little River <span>90 beds</span></li><li>Legacy of North Myrtle Beach <span>80 beds</span></li><li>River Park Senior Living <span>90 beds</span></li></ul><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;has=one_level&amp;city=Little+River" data-head="One-level houses in Little River, every room on one floor"></div></div><div class="sl-town"><h3>Pawleys Island<span>2 homes, 179 beds</span></h3><p>In Georgetown County. The Lakes at Litchfield, a continuing care campus, is here.</p><p class="sl-hosp"><strong>Nearest main hospital:</strong> Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital, about 19 minutes</p><ul class="sl-homes"><li>Arbor Landing at Pawleys <span>100 beds</span></li><li>Lakes at Litchfield Assisted Living <span>79 beds</span></li></ul><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;has=one_level&amp;city=Pawleys+Island" data-head="One-level houses in Pawleys Island, every room on one floor"></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times are our measurement: the middle of 60 houses in each place, with no traffic, to the nearest of five main hospitals. <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/professionals/healthcare-quality/find-facility" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state's facility map</a> shows each home's license and address.</p><ul class="sl-list"><li><strong>North Myrtle Beach.</strong> No licensed assisted living home has a North Myrtle Beach address. Three are within a mile of its city limits, in a straight line. One is in Little River, named Legacy of North Myrtle Beach, and two are in Myrtle Beach, near the city's south end.</li><li><strong>Small homes and large ones.</strong> The smallest homes have 8 beds and the largest has 142. Horry County has the third most licensed assisted living beds in South Carolina, after Greenville and Charleston.</li><li><strong>A plan for hurricanes.</strong> Every licensed assisted living home keeps a written disaster and evacuation plan, made with the county emergency agency and updated yearly. A resident or the resident's responsible party may ask to see it.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More on each hospital is on our <a href="/buyers/relocating/healthcare/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach healthcare page</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Tour the towns before you choose a home</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us where the family lives now and what care is needed. We show you the towns, the care homes in each, and the homes for sale around them.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us plan a day of tours</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="memory-care"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Memory care and nursing homes">Memory care and nursing homes around Myrtle Beach</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the state's facility map, 14 of Horry County's 20 licensed assisted living homes are marked for Alzheimer care, and 13 are marked with an Alzheimer unit.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County has 8 licensed nursing homes with 824 beds. Three are in Conway and three in Myrtle Beach, with one each in Murrells Inlet and Loris. Seven of the eight are certified for both Medicare and Medicaid, and one for Medicare only. Certification is not a promise of an open Medicaid bed.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county also has 3 licensed adult day care centers, in Myrtle Beach, Conway and Loris, and a 36-bed hospice house in Myrtle Beach. <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/care-compare/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medicare's Care Compare</a> has a page for each nursing home.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who pays for long-term care</h3><ul class="sl-list"><li><strong>Medicare does not.</strong> Medicare and most health insurance, including Medigap, do not pay for long-term care, in a nursing home or at home. Medicaid may, for people who meet the state's rules.</li><li><strong>South Carolina's Optional State Supplementation (OSS)</strong> helps people 65 or older, blind or disabled, whose income and savings are under its limits. It pays toward a licensed assisted living home enrolled in OSS, for a person with an approved OSS slot.</li><li><strong>OSS is not Medicaid.</strong> It is a separate state program, run by the <a href="https://www.scdhhs.gov/resources/programs-and-initiatives/long-term-living/optional-state-supplementation-oss" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">South Carolina Department of Health and Human Services</a>.</li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="continuing-care"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Continuing care">Continuing care: two licensed campuses on the Grand Strand</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina licenses 33 continuing care retirement communities. Two are on the Grand Strand: Brightwater in Myrtle Beach and The Lakes at Litchfield in Pawleys Island.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A continuing care retirement community offers, under one contract, an apartment or a cottage and access to a range of long-term care as a resident's needs change. The resident pays an entrance fee, which holds the resident's place.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Under South Carolina law, the person who signs has four protections:</p><ul class="sl-list"><li><strong>The refund.</strong> The contract must say what part of the entrance fee is refundable.</li><li><strong>30 days to cancel.</strong> The resident may cancel within 30 days of signing. The refund is what was paid, less the community's costs and, if the home was ready to move into, a daily rate from the eighth day.</li><li><strong>A disclosure statement.</strong> By the time the contract is signed or any money is paid, whichever comes first, the community must give one.</li><li><strong>A check of the finances.</strong> The state checks a community's finances before it grants a license.</li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="buying"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Buying a home">When does buying a home still make sense?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a couple or a parent who does not need daily care yet, a smaller home here can cost far less each year. A one-level house or a condo with an elevator keeps every room within reach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the city limits, a $400,000 house you live in costs about $1,380 a year in county tax and stormwater fee at 65. Insurance and any HOA fee are extra. A year of assisted living costs about $70,200. The tax rules at 65 are on our <a href="/buyers/retirees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">retiring to Myrtle Beach page</a>.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach, by wheelchair</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County lends beach wheelchairs free on the beaches it runs. Ask at least two days ahead; chairs are limited. In <a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach</a>, special beach wheelchairs are available through the town's police department, and five beach accesses have wheelchair access.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the Surfside Beach Pier, labelled, running from a wide beach into a green ocean, with parking lots and rows of beach houses behind the sand" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>The Surfside Beach Pier from the air. The pier is one of the town's five beach accesses with wheelchair access.</figcaption></figure><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=house&amp;has=one_level" data-head="One-level houses along the Grand Strand, every room on one floor"></div><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=condo&amp;has=elevator_building" data-head="Condos in elevator buildings"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For neighborhoods that are age-restricted, with their own clubs and HOA fees, compare the <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55+ communities around Myrtle Beach</a>. What a home costs to own each year is on our <a href="/buyers/cost-to-own/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">cost of owning page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="selling"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Selling the house">How do you sell the house and move to the right-size home?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We sell a house here, find the next home, and time the two so the money is ready for the move.</p><ul class="sl-list"><li><strong>We price the house from recorded sales.</strong> An agent picks the sales most like it. Our <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">home value page</a> shows what homes sold for by area.</li><li><strong>We plan the order.</strong> Sell first, buy first, or both close together: our guide to <a href="/sell/sell-or-buy-first/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">selling or buying first</a> weighs each.</li><li><strong>We handle it from a distance.</strong> A parent can stay put while we list and show the house. Our page on <a href="/sell/out-of-state-buyers/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">selling from out of state</a> covers the steps.</li><li><strong>We show what you keep.</strong> Our <a href="/sell/net-proceeds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">net proceeds page</a> works out the cash left after the loan and closing costs. Our <a href="/sell/capital-gains/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">capital gains page</a> shows when the gain on a home you lived in is taxed.</li><li><strong>We find the next home.</strong> A one-level house, a condo with an elevator, or a home near the care a parent uses.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An agent at Chapter3 worked with a client household from New York. They sold a $1 million house with more than $20,000 a year in property tax. They bought a $700,000 house here with about $3,200 a year in tax. That is one household's result, not a promise.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the house is in another state, an agent there lists it. We work out the timing with you, so the money from that sale is ready for the move here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="senior-living-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Senior living questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does Medicare pay for assisted living in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Medicare and Medigap do not pay for long-term care, in a nursing home or in the community. Medicaid can, for those who qualify.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is there help paying for assisted living in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, for some people. A state program called Optional State Supplementation helps pay for a licensed assisted living home enrolled in it, for a person with an approved slot. It is for people 65 or older, blind or disabled, under its income and savings limits. It is not Medicaid.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do assisted living homes near Myrtle Beach have a hurricane plan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Each licensed assisted living home must have a written evacuation plan, made with the county's emergency agency and updated every year. A resident or the resident's responsible party can ask to read it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is independent living licensed in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. South Carolina licenses assisted living and nursing homes, but it has no license for independent living with no care.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What does adult day care cost in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About $72 a day at the middle, or about $1,560 a month at five days a week. Horry County has 3 licensed adult day care centers, in Myrtle Beach, Conway and Loris.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is memory care in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">There is no published local figure: the cost survey does not price memory care on its own. Prices differ from one home to the next.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.carescout.com/cost-of-care" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CareScout 2025 survey</a>, <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/professionals/healthcare-quality/find-facility" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC DPH facility map</a>, <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/professionals/healthcare-quality/licensed-facilities-professionals/community-residential-care" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DPH residential care</a>, <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/sites/scdph/files/Library/00343-ENG-CR.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DPH sheet 00343</a>, <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/sites/scdph/files/Library/Regulations/R.60-84.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Reg. 60-84</a>, <a href="https://consumer.sc.gov/business-resourceslaws/licensing/ccrcs" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Consumer Affairs</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t37c011.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 37-11</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t44c007.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 44-7</a>, <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/long-term-care" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medicare.gov</a>, <a href="https://www.scdhhs.gov/resources/programs-and-initiatives/long-term-living/optional-state-supplementation-oss" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDHHS OSS</a>, <a href="https://data.cms.gov/provider-data/dataset/4pq5-n9py" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CMS nursing homes</a>, <a href="https://hudgis-hud.opendata.arcgis.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD assisted housing</a>, <a href="https://resources.hud.gov/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD Resource Locator</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/about-our-beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County beaches</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/200/Beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surfside Beach</a>. Costs are medians from CareScout's 2025 Cost of Care Survey. Our counts: the state's licensed facility list, by mailing address, and its Total Licensed Beds.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The Surfside Beach Pier from the air. The pier is one of the town's five beach accesses with wheelchair access. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from one NOAA aerial photo, resized it, adjusted the colors and added a label.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The Surfside Beach Pier from the air","caption":"The Surfside Beach Pier from the air. The pier is one of the town's five beach accesses with wheelchair access.","description":"Aerial photo of the Surfside Beach Pier, labelled, running from a wide beach into a green ocean, with parking lots and rows of beach houses behind the sand","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"NOAA National Geodetic Survey"},"creditText":"NOAA National Geodetic Survey, public domain","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (NOAA National Geodetic Survey)","license":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm","acquireLicensePage":"https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/","isBasedOn":"https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"the pier at 11 South Ocean Boulevard, Surfside Beach, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Sell the house, find the right-size home.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Tell us what care is needed and where. We price the house, plan the move and find the next home.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask us to plan it</a></div></section></main>
