 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the sun rise over the ocean in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. From central Myrtle Beach south to Garden City, the sun rises over open sea every morning of the year. Farther north, from Windy Hill to Cherry Grove, it comes up over the shore on many mornings around June."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest waterfront in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A condo in an oceanfront building, which sold for about $200,000 at the middle. For a house, it is a lake or pond: every waterfront house for sale under $300,000 was on one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much more does a waterfront home cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the beach, a house resold for about $2.2 million at the middle, against about $615,000 for houses nearby off the water. On the Intracoastal Waterway, a house sold for about twice the houses nearby. On Garden City's salt marsh, a house sold for about twice the other houses on that side of the beach road."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I build a dock on my waterfront lot?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On salt water, yes, if the lot and the creek are wide enough and the state issues a permit. Lots created since 1993 need 75 feet of frontage at the marsh edge."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I keep a boat without a dock?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A deeded boat slip is another way, and most of the slips sold as real estate in Horry County are in Little River."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need flood insurance on a waterfront home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A federally regulated lender requires it in FEMA's high-risk zone. Nearly every lot on the beach, the Cherry Grove channels and the Waccamaw River reaches that zone. On the Intracoastal Waterway, about 3 in 10 lots are wholly outside it."}}]}</script>
