 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are HOA fees a waste of money?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not when the fee buys what you would pay for anyway. In The Farm at Carolina Forest, the HOA spends about $43 of each home's $107 monthly fee on cable TV, and trash pickup is the next largest line."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do HOA homes sell for more in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not by asking prices. Newer houses with an HOA fee list for less a square foot than newer houses without one in all 10 Horry County ZIP codes we could compare."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a gated community worth the HOA fee?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if you want a staffed gate. One post staffed all year costs about $132,500 in a guard's pay alone, about $22 a home a month if 500 homes share it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can an HOA raise its fees in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. State law puts no cap on dues or special assessments. The limits are in each community's own recorded rules and bylaws."}}]}</script>
