ainst what the same things cost alone.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A homeowners association (HOA) fee is worth it when it buys things you would pay for anyway, for less than they cost alone. In The Farm at Carolina Forest, the HOA spends about $43 of each home's $107 monthly fee on cable TV.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The budget's pool line there comes to about $63 a home a year, less than one adult's year at a city pool. The trade-off is room: newer houses with a fee sit on smaller lots, and few houses with a fee list a place to park a boat.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Found a home with an HOA fee? We find out what it buys.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us price a home's fee</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#what-it-buys" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What a fee buys</a></li><li><a href="#pool" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The pool</a></li><li><a href="#beach-club" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Beach clubs</a></li><li><a href="#gate" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Gates</a></li><li><a href="#condo" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Condo fees</a></li><li><a href="#value" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Property value</a></li><li><a href="#give-up" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What you give up</a></li><li><a href="#we-check" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What we check</a></li><li><a href="#common-questions-about-hoa-fees" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Common questions about HOA fees</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-it-buys"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What a fee buys">What does an HOA fee pay for?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Farm at Carolina Forest is a neighborhood of 1,571 homes outside any city limit, with a Myrtle Beach mailing address. Its main HOA fee is $107 a month, and its newest budget keeps it at $107.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA buys cable TV from Spectrum for its homes, the largest line in the budget at about 40 cents of each dollar. Trash pickup, which the HOA hires, is the next largest.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="The Farm spends about $43 of each home's $107 fee on cable TV"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">The Farm spends about $43 of each home's $107 fee on cable TV</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Budget line</span><span role="columnheader">Each home's share a month</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Cable TV</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$43</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Trash pickup</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.312" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$13</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Common-area landscaping and ponds</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.287" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$12</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The management company</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.216" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$9</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Power for shared areas</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.156" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$7</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Savings for future projects</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.13" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$6</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The two pools</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.122" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$5</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Insurance</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.061" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$3</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All other lines</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.239" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$10</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Each home's share of the HOA's newest approved budget is about $108 a month: $107 from the fee, and the rest from transfer fees, rent and key cards.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cable TV and trash pickup take about half of each home's share. If you would pay for cable TV anyway, about $43 of the fee is a bill you already have.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rest keeps up the shared land and its ponds, two pools, an activity center and a clubhouse with a fitness room. It also pays the company that runs the HOA.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From April 15 to October 15, both pools stay open until 9 p.m., so a swim after work is part of what the fee buys.</p><figure class="hb-ph"><img src="/images/2026-11-b/hoa-benefits/the-farm-pool-from-above-2026-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-b/hoa-benefits/the-farm-pool-from-above-2026-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-b/hoa-benefits/the-farm-pool-from-above-2026-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Farm at Carolina Forest from above in winter, labelled: a large curving blue pool with a wide deck and two palm islands beside a dark pond, and a white-roofed activity center at the lower left"><figcaption>The Farm's large pool and activity center from above. The HOA keeps up two pools. <span class="cr">Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, public domain. Labels by Chapter3 Realty.</span></figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Other communities put other services in the fee. In Del Webb North Myrtle Beach, the fee is $315 a month on most homes for sale or recently sold. The builder lists lawn care and a 175-channel TV package in it.</p><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>On The Farm's north edge</b>The state bought land there for a nature preserve. That land holds habitat for the Venus flytrap.</li><li><b>The trade-off</b>No private pool on a lot. A boat, trailer, camper or RV may be kept outside only with the HOA's written approval; pickups and SUVs are fine.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our page about <a href="/hoa/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach HOA fees</a> shows what fees include for a typical house, townhouse or condo. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/the-farm/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to The Farm</a> covers daily life there.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="the-farm" data-name="The Farm" data-head="Homes in The Farm, with pools open until 9 p.m. all season"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=The%20Farm">Get the homes for sale in The Farm<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="pool"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The pool">Is the pool worth the HOA fee?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pool is worth it for a household that swims. The pool line in the budget comes to about $63 a home a year at The Farm, and about $77 at Myrtle Trace with its ponds.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A year at a city pool and gym in Myrtle Beach costs an adult aged 18 to 54 $175 to $295. North Myrtle Beach's Aquatic and Fitness Center costs $555 for one adult.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="A year of pool: a home's share of the pool line, or one adult's city pass"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">A year of pool: a home's share of the pool line, or one adult's city pass</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Pool, what it covers or the senior price</span><span role="columnheader">A year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The Farm, each home's share</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">two outdoor pools</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.114" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$63</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Trace, each home's share</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">the pool and fifteen ponds</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.139" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$77</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach city pass, resident</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">$125 at 55 and up</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.315" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$175</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach city pass, nonresident</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">$210 at 55 and up</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.532" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$295</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach center pass</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">$465 at 62 and up</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$555</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>HOA rows: the pool line in each budget, divided by its homes, before power, insurance and repair savings. City rows: one adult aged 18 to 54 (24 and up in North Myrtle Beach), with a gym.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two are not the same thing. A city pass is for one person and adds a gym. The Farm's pools are outdoors and open from mid-April to mid-October.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Myrtle Trace: fifteen ponds to fish</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Trace is a 55+ community whose HOA owns 42 acres of common land besides its roads, with fifteen ponds. Residents and their house guests may fish the ponds from common land; every fish is released.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA uses its $95 monthly fee to keep up the pool, the clubhouse, the roads, the common areas and the ponds. Large pond and pool repairs come from its reserve fund, on top of the pool line.</p><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>On the ponds</b>Swimming and recreational boats are not allowed.</li><li><b>In the driveway</b>Trucks go in the garage when not in use. Boats, campers and RVs park by permit at the clubhouse lot.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We have a full <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/myrtle-trace/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to Myrtle Trace</a>.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="myrtle-trace" data-name="Myrtle Trace" data-head="Myrtle Trace homes with fifteen ponds to fish"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Trace">Get the homes for sale in Myrtle Trace<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the budget behind the fee</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Name the community. We get its budget and show you what each home's share pays for.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us get the budget</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="beach-club"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Beach clubs">Is a beach club worth a higher HOA fee?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A beach club is worth a higher fee for an owner who will use it often. Two places here have one: the Grande Dunes Ocean Club for Del Webb at Grande Dunes owners, and a private ocean cabana in parts of Barefoot Resort. A Del Webb house lists a fee of about $400 a month, against about $95 for a typical house here.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Del Webb at Grande Dunes: the Ocean Club</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Grande Dunes master association says a Grande Dunes homeowner gets a household membership in the Grande Dunes Ocean Club. It lists Del Webb among its neighborhoods.</p><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>The Ocean Club</b>A large outdoor pool and whirlpool, private beach access, and classes, clubs, dining and entertainment.</li><li><b>The amenity center</b>The community's posted rules list indoor and outdoor pools, a fitness center, tennis, pickleball and bocce courts and a day dock, with a lifestyle director.</li><li><b>Not allowed</b>Sheds and above-ground pools.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What you pay: every owner pays a mandatory Beach Club fee to the Grande Dunes master association, on top of the association's own assessments.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Del Webb house lists a fee of about $400 a month. We check what that figure covers, and what the master association bills on top, before you offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb at Grande Dunes guide</a> covers the rest of the community.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="del-webb-grande-dunes" data-name="Del Webb at Grande Dunes" data-head="Del Webb homes with a membership in the Grande Dunes Ocean Club"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Del%20Webb%20at%20Grande%20Dunes">Get the homes for sale in Del Webb at Grande Dunes<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Barefoot Resort: an ocean cabana and a waterway pool</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Barefoot Resort's residential association gives owners in its member neighborhoods a private cabana on the ocean in North Myrtle Beach, and more:</p><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>The Beach Cabana</b>Owner parking and a beach gate opened by key fob, a kitchen, showers, an elevator and staff attendants.</li><li><b>A beach shuttle</b>In season, a shuttle takes owners to and from the beach.</li><li><b>The North Tower pool</b>Beside the Intracoastal Waterway, it holds about 356,000 gallons.</li><li><b>The Residents' Club</b>For most single-family neighborhoods: a 5,000-square-foot club with a pool, a weight room, a library, tennis and pickleball courts and a lifestyle director.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condos for sale in Barefoot list a typical fee of about $570 a month. Houses in its Leatherleaf section list $385 to $398. Not every Barefoot neighborhood belongs to the residential association, so we check which one a home is in.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="barefoot-resort" data-name="Barefoot Resort" data-head="Barefoot homes with an ocean cabana and a waterway pool for members"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Barefoot%20Resort">Get the homes for sale in Barefoot Resort<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our guides to <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55+ communities</a> and <a href="/buyers/gated-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">gated communities</a> compare the other clubs one by one.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="gate"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Gates">Is a gated community worth the HOA fee?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A gated community is worth the fee if you want a gate with a guard, because a shared fee splits the cost among many homes. One household alone would pay all of it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the Myrtle Beach metro area, security guards earned a middle wage of $15.13 an hour in the latest federal wage survey. At that wage, one gate staffed day and night costs this much:</p><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>8,760 hours a year</b>A guard at the gate every hour of the year.</li><li><b>About $132,500 a year</b>The guard's pay alone, before taxes, benefits or a security company's margin.</li><li><b>About $22 a home a month</b>That pay shared by 500 homes, as an example.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Dye Estates, inside Barefoot Resort, owners and their guests are greeted by the security staff at the front guardhouse.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A gate controls who drives in. We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. Our <a href="/buyers/gated-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to gated communities</a> compares the gated places here.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Add up the gate, the club and the HOA</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the home. We find every fee on it, the master association's too, and what each one pays for.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us find every fee on a home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="condo"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Condo fees">Are condo fees worth it in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condo fees are usually worth it, because owners pay together through the fee for what no one owner could buy alone.</p><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>The building's insurance</b>South Carolina law requires a condo association to insure the property. Each owner may still insure their own unit.</li><li><b>The roof</b>In a condo, the roof belongs to all the owners together, and its repair is a shared expense. Owners of a one-family house in the South Atlantic states, which include South Carolina, who replaced a roof paid a middle of more than $10,000.</li><li><b>A policy lenders accept</b>For a loan sold to Fannie Mae, the building's deductible may be no more than 5 percent of its coverage. When it is charged per unit, the limit is $50,000 a unit. If the policy falls outside those limits, fewer of your buyers can get a loan there. Our page on <a href="/hoa/master-insurance-ho6/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the building's policy and your own</a> explains both.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our page about <a href="/hoa/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach HOA fees</a> explains why condo fees are high here. The fee in each community is in our list of <a href="/hoa/fees-by-neighborhood/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA fees in 382 neighborhoods</a>. Fees building by building are on our <a href="/invest/condo-buildings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">oceanfront condo buildings</a> page.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="value"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Property value">Do HOAs increase property value in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not in asking prices. Here, newer houses with an HOA fee list for less a square foot than houses without one. Of houses for sale built in 2000 or later in Horry County ZIP codes, those with a fee list for a middle of about $205 a square foot. Those with no fee list for about $274.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The house with no fee also sits on more land: about half an acre, against about a fifth of an acre with a fee.</p><figure class="c3-gchart hb-pc"><table class="hb-tab"><caption>Newer houses with an HOA fee list for less a square foot, near the beach and far from it</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Distance from the beach</th><th scope="col">Middle asking price a square foot</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><span class="n">Under 1 mile from the beach</span><span class="f">Lot: 0.12 acre with a fee, 0.16 acre without</span></th><td><span class="hb-ln"><span class="b" style="--f:0.815" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$340 with a fee</span></span><span class="hb-ln nf"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$417 no fee</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="n">1 to 3 miles</span><span class="f">Lot: 0.17 acre with a fee, 0.24 acre without</span></th><td><span class="hb-ln"><span class="b" style="--f:0.612" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$255 with a fee</span></span><span class="hb-ln nf"><span class="b" style="--f:0.715" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$298 no fee</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="n">3 to 10 miles</span><span class="f">Lot: 0.20 acre with a fee, 0.66 acre without</span></th><td><span class="hb-ln"><span class="b" style="--f:0.477" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$199 with a fee</span></span><span class="hb-ln nf"><span class="b" style="--f:0.54" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$225 no fee</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="n">Over 10 miles</span><span class="f">Lot: 0.23 acre with a fee, 1 acre without</span></th><td><span class="hb-ln"><span class="b" style="--f:0.427" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$178 with a fee</span></span><span class="hb-ln nf"><span class="b" style="--f:0.547" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$228 no fee</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption>Houses for sale built in 2000 or later, in Horry County ZIP codes. Middle asking price a square foot. Distance in a straight line. The two middle bands have few houses with no fee (43 and 36).</figcaption></figure><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>ZIP code by ZIP code</b>Counting houses of every age, those with a fee list for less a square foot in 12 of the 13 ZIP codes with enough of both. Socastee is the one exception. Among newer houses only, it is 10 of 10.</li><li><b>What a national study found</b>A 2019 national study of mortgage records found that houses in HOAs sold for at least 4 percent more, on average, than similar houses outside them. Our count here compares asking prices and does not show a cause.</li><li><b>Often there is no choice</b>Of newer houses for sale 1 to 3 miles from the beach, 91 in 100 list an HOA fee. From 3 to 10 miles, 96 in 100 do.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the land and no HOA fee?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us where you want to live. We send you houses there with no HOA fee, with the lot size of each.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us for houses with no HOA</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="give-up"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What you give up">What do you give up in an HOA?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In an HOA you give up room, some freedom and some say over the money. In return, every neighbor follows the same rules you do.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether the dues come off your taxes is on our page on <a href="/hoa/tax-deductible/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA fees and taxes</a>.</p><ul class="hb-plain"><li><b>Room for a boat or an RV</b>Our listing feed covers the Grand Strand from Pawleys Island into North Carolina. In it, about 3 in 100 houses for sale with an HOA fee list parking for an RV or a boat. With no fee, about 3 in 10 do. Houses with a fee list a boat ramp more often, 9 in 100 against 2. Our page on <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">homes with no HOA</a> shows where those houses are.</li><li><b>Things you cannot build or park</b>Each community above has rules against something: a private pool, a shed or a boat in the driveway. The biggest mistake we see buyers from New York make is not checking that the community's rules fit how they live. That means the HOA rules on boats, golf carts, rentals and pools.</li><li><b>No cap in state law</b>South Carolina's HOA law and condo law put no cap on dues, on a special assessment or on <a href="/hoa/violations-and-fines/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">a fine</a>. The limits are in each community's own recorded rules and bylaws. The Farm's recorded rules cap a yearly increase in the base fee at 20 percent. More on <a href="/hoa/dues-increases/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how much an HOA can raise dues</a>.</li><li><b>A low fee can mean thin savings</b>If an HOA saves too little for repairs, owners can face a <a href="/hoa/special-assessments/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">special assessment</a> later, a one-time bill to each owner. Our page on <a href="/hoa/reserves/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA reserves</a> covers how much an HOA should save.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What do owners here complain to the state about?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of the concerns the state names, the most common, in 36 of 100 complaints, was that the HOA did not follow or enforce its own rules. Maintenance and repairs came next, in 30 of 100.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What Horry County owners complain to the state about their HOA"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What Horry County owners complain to the state about their HOA</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Concern</span><span role="columnheader">Complaints that name it</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Did not follow or enforce its own rules</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.361" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">36 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Maintenance or repairs</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.303" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">30 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Did not answer a request to see documents</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.202" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">20 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">How the HOA spends its money</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.178" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">18 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Disagrees with the fees or a special assessment</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.175" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">18 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Did not tell owners about board actions</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.132" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">13 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Did not produce financial statements</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.118" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">12 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Board elections</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.111" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">11 in 100</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>416 complaints from Horry County to SC Consumer Affairs, 2022 to 2025. A complaint can name several concerns. About 22 in 100 named one the state files as other.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our page on <a href="/hoa/south-carolina-hoa-laws/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">South Carolina HOA laws</a> explains where an owner can take a dispute.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Send us the rules before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us about the boat, the truck, the dog or the rental plan. We read the community's rules against it and tell you what they allow.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us read the rules</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="we-check"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What we check">What do we check before you buy a home with an HOA?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We read six things before you make an offer, and tell you what each one means for you.</p><ol class="hb-plain"><li><b>The budget, per home</b>What each line buys, and which of those bills you would pay anyway.</li><li><b>The reserves</b>How much the HOA has saved for future repairs, and its reserve study if it has one.</li><li><b>The building's insurance</b>For a condo, the master policy and its deductible.</li><li><b>The recorded rules</b>Against your boat, truck, pets, pool or rental plans.</li><li><b>Who runs the board</b>The owners or still the builder. More on <a href="/hoa/developer-control-turnover/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">when the builder hands over the HOA</a>.</li><li><b>What the HOA charges when you buy</b>More on <a href="/hoa/estoppel-and-transfer-fees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA transfer fees at closing</a>.</li></ol><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not publish an opinion about any named association. We tell you what its papers say.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="common-questions-about-hoa-fees"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Common questions about HOA fees</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are HOA fees a waste of money?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not when the fee buys what you would pay for anyway. In The Farm at Carolina Forest, the HOA spends about $43 of each home's $107 monthly fee on cable TV, and trash pickup is the next largest line.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do HOA homes sell for more in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not by asking prices. Newer houses with an HOA fee list for less a square foot than newer houses without one in all 10 Horry County ZIP codes we could compare.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a gated community worth the HOA fee?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only if you want a staffed gate. One post staffed all year costs about $132,500 in a guard's pay alone, about $22 a home a month if 500 homes share it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can an HOA raise its fees in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. State law puts no cap on dues or special assessments. The limits are in each community's own recorded rules and bylaws.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.farmatcarolinaforest.com/uploads/documents_page/The%20Farm%20@%20Carolina%20Forest%20HOA%20-%20Budget%20Summary%20Report%20NEW%20DNU.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Farm budget</a>, <a href="https://myrtletracesc.org/wp-content/uploads/AnnualMeetingCommitteeReports/2026/2026AAnnualMeetingDocuments.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Trace budget</a>, <a href="https://myrtletracesc.org/wp-content/uploads/MTHOA-Policies-2025/MTHOAPropertyCommitteeGuidelines2026.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Trace rules</a>, <a href="https://www.delwebbatgrandedunes.com/ResourceCenter/Download/48372~3083079" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Del Webb declaration</a>, <a href="https://grandedunescommunities.sites.townsq.io/2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grande Dunes Ocean Club</a>, <a href="https://www.barefoothoa.com/amenities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Barefoot association</a>, <a href="https://www.bls.gov/oes/current/oes_34820.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS wages</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/recreation_center_memberships.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach passes</a>, <a href="https://afc.nmb.us/174/Membership" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach passes</a>, <a href="https://econpapers.repec.org/RePEc:eee:juecon:v:112:y:2019:i:c:p:1-15" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Clarke and Freedman</a>, <a href="https://www.consumer.sc.gov/HOA-reports" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Consumer Affairs</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c030.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-30</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c031.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-31</a>, <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b7-3-03/master-property-insurance-requirements-project-developments" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae B7-3-03</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/ahs/2023/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census AHS</a>. Our counts: houses for sale in our listing feed, asking prices; budget lines divided by each HOA's homes; the gate at 500 homes is an example.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Legal notice.</strong> Chapter3 Realty Corp is a licensed South Carolina real estate brokerage, not a law firm or a tax adviser. This page is general information, not legal or tax advice. We do not publish an opinion about any named association.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Is this HOA fee worth it for you?</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Call 854.333.2135, or send us the home or the community. We get the budget and the rules, and tell you what the fee buys and what it rules out.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us review the fee</a></div></section></main>
