 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are HOA documents public record in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The recorded ones are: the declaration, the bylaws, their amendments and the rules. In Horry County the index is online; we pull the pages at the county for you. The rest come from the association."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I back out of buying a house because of the HOA documents?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not under a South Carolina law. Your contract's review time is when to act. In Virginia, Maryland and Florida, a buyer has a set number of days by law."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to get HOA documents?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"South Carolina law has no deadline for them, so it depends on the association. That is why we ask the manager for the papers and a date as soon as you are under contract."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays for HOA documents in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No South Carolina law caps the association's fee for them or names an amount. We find out what the manager charges before the papers are ordered, so the cost is known up front."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the seller have to tell me there is an HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, unless the sale is exempt, such as the first sale of a new home. The seller's disclosure form asks, and a yes brings the one-page HOA addendum. A missing form does not undo the contract."}}]}</script>
