></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.987" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$154</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Waterway Palms Plantation</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Pool, clubhouse, tennis</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$156</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>The middle monthly fee in the Carolina Forest neighborhoods of houses with the most homes for sale. Pick Carolina Forest in the town list to see them all.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest guide</a> covers the area itself.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Waterbridge: a pool complex, and lakes through the neighborhood</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://waterbridgehoa.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Waterbridge</a> has over 80 acres of lakes and natural areas, a swimming pool complex, pocket parks and a clubhouse. Every house for sale there lists an HOA fee, and nearly all list $150 a month.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-d/hoa-fees-by-neighborhood/waterbridge-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-d/hoa-fees-by-neighborhood/waterbridge-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-d/hoa-fees-by-neighborhood/waterbridge-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Waterbridge from above: a pool complex and clubhouse, labelled, inside a circle drive, with streets of houses all around" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Waterbridge from above: the pools and clubhouse inside a circle of streets.</figcaption></figure><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="subdivision=Waterbridge&amp;type=house" data-head="Waterbridge houses, with the pool complex and lakes"></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The Farm at Carolina Forest: two pools for $107</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Farm's HOA fee is $107 a month. Its amenities include two pools, an activity center, a clubhouse with a fitness room, a basketball court and a playground. Most of its houses for sale list $107, and the others $100 or $110.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-b/hoa-benefits/the-farm-pool-from-above-2026-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-b/hoa-benefits/the-farm-pool-from-above-2026-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-b/hoa-benefits/the-farm-pool-from-above-2026-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="The Farm at Carolina Forest from above in winter, labelled: a large curving blue pool with a wide deck and two palm islands beside a dark pond, and a white-roofed activity center at the lower left by a curving road" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Farm's large pool and its activity center, from above.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Owners in two of its neighborhoods pay a second fee. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/the-farm/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to The Farm</a> has both.</p><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="subdivision=Carolina+Forest+-+The+Farm&amp;type=house" data-head="Houses in The Farm, with two pools and an activity center"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="two-fees"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Two fees or none">Two fees, or no HOA fee at all</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Close to 9 in 10 homes for sale in these neighborhoods list an HOA fee, outside the campground and leased-land communities. Some owners pay a second fee, and some pay a lot rent instead.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A second fee on top of the HOA</h3><ul class="hf-list"><li><strong>The Farm at Carolina Forest.</strong> Owners in The Orchards pay about $225 to $255 a month in all. In Planters Point, it is about $450 to $500.</li><li><strong><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb at Grande Dunes</a>.</strong> The fee is about $400 a month for a house and about $445 for a villa. Every owner also pays a <a href="https://www.delwebbatgrandedunes.com/ResourceCenter/Download/48372~3083079" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">mandatory Beach Club fee</a> to the Grande Dunes master association, on top of that.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A listing may show one fee or both. Our page on <a href="/hoa/hoa-vs-poa/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOAs and POAs</a> explains a neighborhood with two associations.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">One community, many names</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some communities appear in the listings under many neighborhood names, each with its own listed fee.</p><ul class="hf-list"><li><strong>Grande Dunes.</strong> Houses in its neighborhoods list from about $232 in Cipriana Park to about $503 in Waterside Pointe.</li><li><strong>Prince Creek and Prince Creek West.</strong> Houses list from about $99 in Longwood Bluffs to $180 in Willow Bay, and $342 in Seasons at Prince Creek West, a 55+ community. Prince Creek West is a <a href="https://www.tollbrothers.com/luxury-homes-for-sale/South-Carolina/Townes-of-Prince-Creek-West" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2,700-acre master plan</a>. Its amenity complex, The Park, has two community pools, sport courts and walking trails.</li><li><strong>Market Common.</strong> Houses list from about $63 in Highlands at Withers Preserve to $220 in Sweetgrass Square, and townhomes about $450 and $490.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Leased land: a lot rent instead of an HOA fee</h3><ul class="hf-list"><li><strong>Ocean Lakes.</strong> Every listing there says there is no HOA. The houses and mobile homes are on <a href="https://www.oceanlakes.com/lodging-2/annual-lease-sales/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2,579 annual lease sites</a> along a mile of oceanfront.</li><li><strong>Lakeside Crossing</strong> in Conway. The homes are on leased land in a 55+ community. There is no HOA, and the lot rent is the monthly cost. More is on our <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55+ communities page</a>.</li><li><strong>Conway Plantation and Crystal Lake.</strong> We read their listings: the homes are on leased land with a monthly lot rent.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The other manufactured-home communities in the table list no HOA fee. Ask about a lot rent before you offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">No HOA fee listed</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In 35 neighborhoods of houses or townhomes, no listing for sale gives a fee. Among them are Hagley Estates in Pawleys Island, Windy Hill Beach in North Myrtle Beach and Pine Lakes in Myrtle Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/plantation-point/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Plantation Point</a>, none of the houses for sale lists a fee, and half say there is no HOA. To shop only homes with no HOA, see our <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">no HOA homes page</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Name the home, and we find every fee it pays.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">The HOA, a master association, a club or a lot rent. We get each one in writing before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us about every fee on a home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="townhomes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Townhomes">Why are townhome HOA fees higher?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fee covers more. In the middle townhome neighborhood the HOA fee is about $250 a month, more than twice the fee for houses. Counted home by home instead, the middle townhouse fee is about $290, as our <a href="/hoa/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach HOA fees guide</a> shows.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What a townhome fee includes</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of the townhouse listings that give a fee, 84 in 100 say it includes lawn care, 72 in 100 trash pickup and 37 in 100 insurance. For houses it is 8, 46 and 4 in 100. Pest control, cable and water and sewer also show up in townhouse listings, and almost never in house listings.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How to compare it with a house</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A townhome fee buys more items, not the same items at a higher price. A house owner usually does those jobs alone and pays for them apart from the HOA. To compare a house fee with a townhome fee, add what you would pay for the same items on the house.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The listing says the fee includes insurance. It does not say which policy. Ask the HOA what its insurance covers and what yours must cover.</p><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="type=townhouse&amp;has=lawn_care_included" data-head="Townhomes where the HOA does the lawn care"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a condo, each oceanfront building's fee is on our <a href="/invest/condo-buildings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condo buildings page</a>. To add the HOA fee to the tax and insurance for a year, use our <a href="/buyers/cost-to-own/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">cost to own page</a>. How much an HOA may raise its fee is on our <a href="/hoa/dues-increases/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">dues increases page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="hoa-fees-by-neighborhood-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">HOA fees by neighborhood: FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the HOA fee in Lakeside Crossing in Conway?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Lakeside Crossing has no HOA fee. The homes are on leased land in a 55+ community, and the lot rent is the monthly cost.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why does a listing's HOA fee differ from the HOA's?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A home's listed fee is what its agent typed for that home. A home in two associations may list one fee or both. We get the HOA's own figure before you offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is the HOA fee part of the monthly cost of a home?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Add it to the property tax and the insurance. Our cost to own page adds them up for a year.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why are townhome HOA fees higher?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fee covers more. Most townhouse listings that give a fee say it includes lawn care and trash pickup, and fewer than 1 in 10 house listings include lawn care. Insurance, pest control and water and sewer also show up far more often for townhouses.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What about condo HOA fees?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our table lists neighborhoods of houses, townhomes and manufactured homes. For a condo for sale that lists a fee, the middle fee is about $650 a month.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://chapter3realty.com/homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CCMLS listings (our count)</a>, <a href="https://waterbridgehoa.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Waterbridge HOA</a>, <a href="https://www.farmatcarolinaforest.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Farm HOA</a>, <a href="https://www.delwebbatgrandedunes.com/ResourceCenter/Download/48372~3083079" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Del Webb at Grande Dunes declaration</a>, <a href="https://www.tollbrothers.com/luxury-homes-for-sale/South-Carolina/Townes-of-Prince-Creek-West" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Toll Brothers, Prince Creek West</a>, <a href="https://www.oceanlakes.com/lodging-2/annual-lease-sales/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ocean Lakes lease sales</a>, <a href="https://www.cresswind-myrtlebeach.com/about-cresswind/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cresswind Myrtle Beach</a>. Our count, November 2026: the monthly HOA fee on each house (detached or semi-detached), townhome and manufactured home for sale, to the dollar, from CCMLS listings in aggregate. 2,585 of the 3,990 such homes for sale we found in South Carolina are in these neighborhoods. A neighborhood is its MLS name.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Waterbridge from above: the pools and clubhouse inside a circle of streets. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service, adjusted the colors and added labels placed from county data.</div><div role="listitem">The Farm's large pool and its activity center, from above. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty joined three NOAA map tiles, cut a close view, brightened the colors and added two labels placed from count