 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Am I grandfathered if my HOA bans rentals after I buy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not by South Carolina law. Neither its HOA law nor its condo law exempts owners who bought before a new rule. Florida has such a law, and South Carolina does not. At The Atrium in Myrtle Beach, a 1998 amendment ended leases of 30 days or less for every unit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does residential use only ban Airbnb?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not by those words alone in the papers we read. North Beach Plantation's residential-use rule says it does not restrict any form of rental, and Sand Dunes Oceanfront Tower allows transient residential use. A South Carolina court reads unclear words the way that least restricts the owner."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can an HOA make my renters register?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if its papers say so. In parts of North Beach Plantation, rental guests not staying with the owner register with the on-site access company. Del Webb at Grande Dunes wants notice of each lease within 10 days, and The Farm at Carolina Forest wants the tenants' names."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What counts as a short-term rental in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For the state's lodging tax, a stay of fewer than 90 days in a row by the same guest. A community's papers can define it differently. Surf Estates treats any use under a year as short-term."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I rent out a home in a 55+ community near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, with the age rule. Del Webb at Grande Dunes asks for a 12-month lease and board approval for a tenant under 55. Seasons at Prince Creek West asks for a one-year lease. At Myrtle Trace, a tenant 55 or older must live there full time."}}]}</script>
