 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are HOA fees tax deductible on my primary residence?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. On a home you live in, HOA and condo fees are a personal cost, like insurance and utilities. They are not a property tax either, because an association, not a government, charges them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are HOA fees deductible on a rental property?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. On a condo you rent out, the dues are a rental expense on Schedule E. On a house in an HOA that you rent out, the dues are a cost of renting it, like insurance and repairs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are HOA fees deductible on a second home I do not rent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. A second home you never rent follows the same rule as a main home. If you rent it for 15 days or more, the rented share of the nights becomes deductible."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I deduct HOA fees if I work from home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not as an employee: an employee gets no home office deduction. A self-employed owner who qualifies splits whole-home costs by the share of the home used for business. The IRS's examples are insurance, utilities and general repairs. Its home office guide does not say whether association dues count, so this page does not say they do."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do HOA special assessments lower capital gains when I sell?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On a condo you live in, an assessment for an improvement is added to your cost basis, which lowers the taxable gain. If you qualify, the first $250,000 of gain on a main home is not taxed, or $500,000 for a married couple filing jointly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do family stays count as personal use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, unless the relative rents it at a fair price as their main home. A stay by you, a co-owner or a relative is a personal night, and so is any night rented below a fair price."}}]}</script>
