 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Myrtle Beach oceanfront condos have the lowest HOA fees?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sands Ocean Club, at a typical $425 a month, where most units for sale are studios. Then Towers on the Grove, about $500 from 3 listings, Anderson Ocean Club, about $570, and Beach Colony, about $595."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why are oceanfront condo HOA fees so high?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The fee pays the building's shared bills. Most listings in oceanfront buildings say it includes water and sewer, internet and insurance, and more than half say it pays the power bill."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you have a dog in a Myrtle Beach oceanfront condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In some buildings. At Beach Colony, Margate Tower, Royale Palms and Ocean Creek, most units for sale allow pets. At Coral Beach, none of the 40 do. We read the building's pet rule before you offer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the tallest condo building in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Margate Tower, in Kingston Plantation. It rises about 330 feet, and it also has the largest units and the highest fee of the oceanfront buildings on this page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Myrtle Beach oceanfront condo buildings have a lazy river?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Fifteen of the buildings on this page have one. You can float all year at Landmark, Bay View, the Caribbean, Monterey Bay, Grande Cayman, Ocean Reef and Avista, where it is indoors or under a roof. Prince Resort's is on its roof."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between a condotel and a timeshare?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A condotel unit is owned whole, like any condo. A timeshare sells the use of a unit for some weeks a year."}}]}</script>
