>Fee a month</span>$840</td><td><span class="l">Fee pays power</span>Most</td><td><span class="l">Pets allowed</span>None</td><td><span class="l">Asking now</span>$310,000</td><td><span class="l">Sold for</span>$260,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Towers on the Grove<span class="c">3 for sale</span></th><td><span class="l">Fee a month</span>$500</td><td><span class="l">Fee pays power</span>2 of 3</td><td><span class="l">Pets allowed</span>None</td><td><span class="l">Asking now</span>$145,000</td><td class="w"><span class="l">Sold for</span>None recorded</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#prince-resort" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Prince Resort</a><span class="c">7 for sale</span></th><td><span class="l">Fee a month</span>$1,035</td><td><span class="l">Fee pays power</span>All</td><td><span class="l">Pets allowed</span>None</td><td><span class="l">Asking now</span>$240,000</td><td><span class="l">Sold for</span>$365,000</td></tr><tr class="none"><th scope="row">Ocean Drive Beach & Golf</th><td colspan="5" class="w">No units for sale this week</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fee and the asking price are typical of the units for sale this week. "Fee pays power" and "Pets allowed" say how many of those units list it. The sale price is typical of the past year's one-unit sales. Myrtle Beach Resort and Ocean Creek record their towers under several names, so we do not count their sales.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-fees-pay"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What fees pay">What does an oceanfront condo HOA fee pay for?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An oceanfront fee pays the building's shared bills. Of every 100 condos for sale in oceanfront buildings, this many listings say the fee includes:</p><ul class="c3-cb-cov"><li><b>97 in 100</b><span>Water and sewer</span></li><li><b>88 in 100</b><span>Internet</span></li><li><b>81 in 100</b><span>Insurance</span></li><li><b>57 in 100</b><span>The power bill</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The power bill changes the most from building to building. At <a href="#landmark-resort" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Landmark</a>, 80 of 93 listings say the fee pays it. In 10 buildings on this page, none of the listings does.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three more things come with the fee:</p><ul class="c3-cb-cov c3-cb-more"><li><b>Insurance</b><span>Which policy the fee pays, and what your own unit policy covers, is on our page on <a href="/hoa/master-insurance-ho6/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the building's policy and yours</a>.</span></li><li><b>Savings</b><span>Part of each fee goes to <a href="/hoa/reserves/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">savings for future repairs</a>. When those run short, owners pay a <a href="/hoa/special-assessments/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">special assessment</a> on top of the fee.</span></li><li><b>At closing</b><span>Buying into one of these buildings usually means a transfer fee to the HOA, and often a few months of dues held at closing, as in any HOA. Our page on <a href="/hoa/estoppel-and-transfer-fees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA fees due at closing</a> explains them.</span></li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">The fee a seller lists can be out of date</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the unit. We get its fee from the HOA, with what the fee pays and any special assessment on the way.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us get the current fee for one unit</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="sales"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Sales by building">Which oceanfront buildings sell the most units?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year, <a href="#sea-mist-resort" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Sea Mist</a> and <a href="#landmark-resort" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Landmark</a> sold the most units. Sea Mist had 64 sales. Two units sold twice, so 62 of its 271 units changed hands, more than 1 in 5. At the typical building on this page, about 1 in 17 did.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Sea Mist and Landmark sold the most units"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Sea Mist and Landmark sold the most units</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Building</span><span role="columnheader">Units sold in the past year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#sea-mist-resort">Sea Mist Resort</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">64 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#landmark-resort">Landmark Resort</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.859" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">55 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#coral-beach-resort">Coral Beach Resort</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.625" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">40 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#compass-cove">Compass Cove</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.609" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">39 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#beach-cove-resort">Beach Cove Resort</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.578" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">37 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#sands-ocean-club">Sands Ocean Club</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.563" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">36 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#bay-watch-resort">Bay Watch Resort</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.547" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">35 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#caravelle-resort">Caravelle Resort</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.5" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">32 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="#sand-dunes-resort">Sand Dunes Resort</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.5" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">32 sales</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Units sold one at a time for $10,000 or more in the past year, from the county's deed records. A unit that sold twice counts twice. Buildings with 30 or more sales.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For an owner who sells later, more sales in the building mean more recent prices to price a unit from. At Towers on the Grove, no unit sold on its own over the past twelve months. Our page on <a href="/sell/sell-my-condo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">selling a condo</a> covers the sale itself.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Selling a unit later?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the building and the unit. We price it from the recorded sales in its own building.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price a unit from its building's sales</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="condotel"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Condo or condotel">Condo, condotel or timeshare: what are you buying on the oceanfront?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most units in these buildings are condos. Three kinds of ownership share the oceanfront:</p><ul class="c3-cb-cov c3-cb-more"><li><b>Condo</b><span>You own the unit, and the owners together own the building through the HOA.</span></li><li><b>Condotel</b><span>A condo in a building run like a hotel, which rents units to guests by the night.</span></li><li><b>Timeshare</b><span>The use of a unit for some weeks a year, not the whole unit.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 94 in 100 condos for sale in oceanfront buildings say short-term rentals are allowed, and we read each building's own rules on renting before you offer. The rules town by town are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a>, and the choice of a building's <a href="/invest/rental-program-vs-airbnb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental program or Airbnb</a> has its own page.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condotel is harder to buy with a loan: Fannie Mae will not buy a loan on a unit in a building run like a hotel. Which loans close on these buildings is on our <a href="/invest/condotel-financing/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condotel financing page</a>, and a lawsuit against the association is on our page on <a href="/buyers/condo-in-litigation/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">buying a condo in litigation</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether an oceanfront condo is a good investment is in our <a href="/invest/condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condo investing guide</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="oceanfront-condo-buildings-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Oceanfront condo buildings FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which Myrtle Beach oceanfront condos have the lowest HOA fees?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Sands Ocean Club, at a typical $425 a month, where most units for sale are studios. Then Towers on the Grove, about $500 from 3 listings, Anderson Ocean Club, about $570, and Beach Colony, about $595.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why are oceanfront condo HOA fees so high?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fee pays the building's shared bills. Most listings in oceanfront buildings say it includes water and sewer, internet and insurance, and more than half say it pays the power bill.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you have a dog in a Myrtle Beach oceanfront condo?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In some buildings. At Beach Colony, Margate Tower, Royale Palms and Ocean Creek, most units for sale allow pets. At Coral Beach, none of the 40 do. We read the building's pet rule before you offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the tallest condo building in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Margate Tower, in Kingston Plantation. It rises about 330 feet, and it also has the largest units and the highest fee of the oceanfront buildings on this page.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which Myrtle Beach oceanfront condo buildings have a lazy river?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Fifteen of the buildings on this page have one. You can float all year at Landmark, Bay View, the Caribbean, Monterey Bay, Grande Cayman, Ocean Reef and Avista, where it is indoors or under a roof. Prince Resort's is on its roof.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the difference between a condotel and a timeshare?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condotel unit is owned whole, like any condo. A timeshare sells the use of a unit for some weeks a year.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">parcels</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">deeds</a>, <a href="https://entp.hud.gov/idapp/html/condlook.cfm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD</a>, <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b4-2.1-03/ineligible-projects" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae</a>, <a href="https://www.landmarkresort.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Landmark</a>, <a href="https://www.oceancreek.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ocean Creek</a>, <a href="https://www.beachcove.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-