 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a seller net sheet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A list of every line on the seller's side of the closing: the price, less the commission, the fees, the tax credit and the payoff. The $350,000 example near the top of this page is one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays title insurance in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The buyer pays both policies, the owner's and the lender's, on the state REALTORS' standard contract. Buyer and seller can agree to something else in writing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the seller need an attorney in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every South Carolina home closing must be supervised by a South Carolina attorney, and a lawyer prepares the seller's deed. When the buyer has a loan for a home they will live in, the buyer picks that attorney, who does not advise you. Your own attorney is your cost."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house before the mortgage is paid off?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The closing pays off the loan out of the sale money, and you get what is left."}}]}</script>
