 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is The Market Common part of Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every home in it is inside the City of Myrtle Beach, so the city's zoning and tax rate apply. Nearly every home has a Myrtle Beach mailing address in ZIP code 29577."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I rent out a Market Common home by the night?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only in the town center. The city's zones for rentals under 90 days include the town center's zoning district, but not the neighborhoods around it. Each HOA's rules also decide, and we read them for the home you pick."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Cresswind a 55-plus community?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kolter Homes built Cresswind as what it called an active adult community, aimed at older buyers. Its rules on who may buy or live there are not published online. We read them for any Cresswind home you are thinking about."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I buy one of the apartments over the shops?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The apartments above the town center's shops are rented by the year. The area's 37 condos are in High Market, south of Valor Park."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do the neighborhoods have pools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the 2023 aerial photo, seven of them have one. Cresswind has a clubhouse with a pool and courts. Emmens Preserve, Belle Harbor, Balmoral, Park Place and The Reserve each have a pool with a pool house or small clubhouse. Withers Preserve has a pool with a pool house in its Sanctuary section."}}]}</script>
