idth="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>Beach by car, about</strong><span class="t">5 min</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>High flood risk</strong><span class="t">62 homes</span></span></li></ul><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero mc-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1099px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="A four-story building with shops on the ground floor and apartments with balconies above, on a street in The Market Common" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: DiscoA340. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: DiscoA340</a></span></div><figcaption>A corner of the town center, with shops on the ground floor.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The Market Common: shops, a lake and a movie theater on the old air base, with about 3,000 homes in the neighborhoods around them.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common is a town center on the old Myrtle Beach Air Force Base. It has about 17 places to eat and drink, shops, a movie theater and a lake. About 3,000 homes stand on its streets and in the neighborhoods around it. The beach is about 5 minutes away by car.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year a typical house there resold for about $525,000, and a townhome for about $375,000. Most houses list an HOA fee of $150 a month or less. Just 62 of about 3,000 homes are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. You will hear planes, but no home is in the area the airport's map marks as too loud for homes.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Want the homes for sale here, sorted by neighborhood?</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us send the list</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#life" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Life here</a></li><li><a href="#homes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Neighborhoods</a></li><li><a href="#prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Prices</a></li><li><a href="#yearly-cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Yearly cost</a></li><li><a href="#flood" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood zones</a></li><li><a href="#airport-noise" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Airport noise</a></li><li><a href="#drives" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Beach and drives</a></li><li><a href="#compare" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Compared</a></li><li><a href="#before" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Before</a></li><li><a href="#the-market-common-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The Market Common FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="life"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Life here">What is it like to live in The Market Common?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town center has shops and restaurants along its streets, with a lake and two parks beside them. Its own directory lists about 17 places to eat and drink, among them P.F. Chang's, Tupelo Honey, Gordon Biersch, CO Sushi, Travinia and Dirty Don's Oyster Bar.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It also has a movie theater, a Barnes & Noble, a bowling and billiards hall, a children's museum, a gym and a yoga studio. Shops include Anthropologie, Pottery Barn, Chico's and J.Jill.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero mc-side" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-grand-park-lake-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-grand-park-lake-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-grand-park-lake-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, (max-width: 1099px) 720px, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="The lake and lawn at Grand Park in The Market Common in the evening" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: DiscoA340. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: DiscoA340</a></span></div><figcaption>The lake in Grand Park, beside the town center's shops. It has a 1.1-mile path around it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Grand Park, with its lake and the path around it, and Valor Park sit beside the shops. They have sports fields, picnic areas, fishing spots and Savannah's Playground, built for children of all abilities.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A normal week at the town center</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town center's calendar has something on most days. In a normal week it lists:</p><ul class="mc-rules" aria-label="A normal week at the town center"><li><strong>Mondays</strong>A mystery movie night at the theater.</li><li><strong>Tuesdays and Thursdays</strong>Free trivia nights at the bowling hall, and on Tuesdays at a restaurant too.</li><li><strong>Wednesdays and Saturdays</strong>Morning tours on electric bikes from the bike shop.</li><li><strong>Saturdays</strong>A farmers market at Valor Park, from April into December.</li><li><strong>Some evenings</strong>Live music at restaurants, such as jazz at Gio's and a band at Gordon Biersch each second Tuesday.</li><li><strong>Twice a year</strong>Art in the Park is held at Valor Park, in April and in November.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which homes are a walk from the shops?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes on the town center's own streets are about an 8-minute walk from the shops, measured from the middle of those streets to Valor Park. From the middle of the larger neighborhoods it is a 20- to 35-minute walk, and about 50 minutes from Belle Harbor.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Minutes on foot to Valor Park, from the middle of each neighborhood"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Minutes on foot to Valor Park, from the middle of each neighborhood</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Neighborhood</span><span role="columnheader">On foot</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The town center's own streets</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.136" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Sweetgrass Square</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.236" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">13 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">High Market (condos)</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.26" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The Reserve</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.365" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">20 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Park Place</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.387" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">21 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Balmoral</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.405" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">22 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Withers Preserve</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.462" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">25 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West Lake</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.493" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">27 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Cresswind</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.531" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">29 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Emmens Preserve</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.631" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">35 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Belle Harbor</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.925" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">50 min</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Walking routes on OpenStreetMap streets and paths. The homes nearest the town center in each neighborhood are closer than its middle.</figcaption></figure><ul class="mc-rules" aria-label="Also near Valor Park"><li><strong>A city gym and a college</strong>From Valor Park, the Crabtree Gymnasium is about 11 minutes on foot, and Horry-Georgetown Technical College's Grand Strand campus about 18.</li><li><strong>Groceries</strong>The Food Lion on South Kings Highway is about a 25-minute walk, just over a mile, or about 5 minutes by car.</li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="homes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Neighborhoods">What are the neighborhoods in The Market Common like?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3,000 homes stand in The Market Common area: about 2,480 houses, 465 townhomes and 37 condos. About 570 are in the town center district, and the rest are in the neighborhoods to its west and north-west.</p><ul class="mc-cards" aria-label="The kinds of home in The Market Common"><li><span class="k">Most of the homes</span><b>A house</b><p>About 2,480 houses. A typical one for sale has 3 or 4 bedrooms and about 2,190 square feet. A house here resold for about $525,000, the middle price, and most list an HOA fee of $150 a month or less.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Market%20Common">Have us find Market Common houses<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></li><li><span class="k">About 1 in 6 homes</span><b>A townhome</b><p>About 465. A townhome shares its side walls with the next one, and a typical one for sale has 2 or 3 bedrooms. About half are on the town center's own streets, where one resold for about $400,000 and each one for sale lists an HOA fee over $300 a month.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Market%20Common">Have us find Market Common townhomes<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></li><li><span class="k">Rare here</span><b>A condo</b><p>Only 37 in the whole area, all in one group called High Market, south of Valor Park. A condo there resold for about $310,000. The apartments above the shops are rented by the year, not sold.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Market%20Common">Ask about Market Common condos<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most neighbors live here all year. About 4 in 5 homes are taxed as their owner's main home. On the town center's streets it is about 2 in 3, so more of those homes are second homes or rentals.</p><figure class="mc-fig"><div class="mc-frame"><svg class="mc-map mc-area-m" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="280 330 1240 760" role="img" aria-labelledby="mc-area-t-m"><title id="mc-area-t-m">Aerial map of The Market Common in Myrtle Beach. The town center, with its lake, Valor Park and rows of townhomes, sits just west of the airport's runway. The larger neighborhoods spread to the west and north-west: Cresswind, The Reserve, Emmens Preserve, Balmoral, Withers Preserve, Park Place, West Lake and Belle Harbor, out to the US 17 Bypass. The beach is to the east, past US 17 Business.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-area-aerial.webp" x="0" y="0" width="2000" height="1299" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M1164.7 896L1161.9 880.2L1183 875.7L1186.2 880.9L1191.4 877.8L1190.9 869.7L1186.1 867.8L1184.4 857.9L1203.6 853.6L1206.7 854.9L1209.1 852.5L1238.1 846.1L1243.5 869.7L1245.4 871.8L1248.8 868.7L1245.5 852L1253.6 851.1L1263.3 899.1L1267.1 901.1L1268.8 897.6L1258 845.5L1266.1 845.6L1278.6 903.8L1268.6 905.7L1266.5 910.2L1257.9 912.1L1254.5 909.9L1251.9 913L1224.5 918.8L1221.4 917.6L1219.2 919.9L1199.7 923.9L1193.8 895.9L1204.8 893.3L1207.3 894.8L1216.6 893.5L1218 891.2L1217.6 884L1213.5 881L1211.1 883.5L1187.5 888L1186.7 890.9L1191.1 912.5L1185.4 915.9L1187 926L1172 929.6L1168.5 914.3L1174.3 910.6L1172 897.8L1170 895.4L1164.7 896ZM1152.9 839.4L1147.5 812.8L1154 811.3L1155.7 808.7L1150.3 793.4L1164.9 789.2L1168 790.2L1191.9 781.6L1194.1 790.5L1196.4 792.4L1225.2 783.8L1229.2 801.2L1231.1 803.2L1234.8 800.1L1247.3 798.3L1249.5 794.4L1255.6 793.5L1262.3 825.2L1