+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a Plantation Point golf course?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The course beside the lots is Myrtlewood Golf Club, with two courses, PineHills and Palmetto. Lots in both Plantation Point and The Landing border it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is Plantation Point Plaza?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Plantation Point Plaza is the shopping center at the US 17 Bypass and 38th Avenue North, with a Food Lion. It is about 8 minutes by car from the middle of Plantation Point and about 3 from The Landing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you walk to the beach from Plantation Point?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not easily. The nearest public beach access is about 2.7 miles away, about an hour on foot or about 9 minutes by car."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I rent out a house in Plantation Point?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"County zoning has no limit on how long a home here may be rented. The recorded restrictions can have one, so we pull them for the house you pick."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need flood insurance in Plantation Point?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No house here is in FEMA's high-risk zone, the zone where a lender requires flood insurance. Where the zone touches 35 lots along the water, it stops short of the houses, so we check each house's flood history before you offer."}}]}</script>
