ight="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>On the waterway</strong><span class="t">58 lots</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8.5 18.5V3.5l8 3.6-8 3.6M3.5 19c0-1.4 3.8-2.5 8.5-2.5s8.5 1.1 8.5 2.5-3.8 2.5-8.5 2.5-8.5-1.1-8.5-2.5z"/><circle cx="16" cy="15.2" r="1.2"/></svg></span><span><strong>On the golf course</strong><span class="t">88 lots</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 14, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Myrtlewood Golf Club, next to Plantation Point, serves food and drink to people who do not play, and it has a patio by the Intracoastal Waterway.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Plantation Point is a neighborhood of 352 houses in Myrtle Beach, between the US 17 Bypass and the Intracoastal Waterway, near 38th Avenue North. The nearest public beach access is about 2.7 miles away.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year a typical house here sold for about $785,000. No home for sale lists a monthly HOA fee. Across the golf course, The Landing at Plantation Point has 139 smaller houses that sold for about $280,000.</p><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:2rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#life" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Life here</a></li><li><a href="#lots" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Water and golf lots</a></li><li><a href="#prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Prices</a></li><li><a href="#hoa" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">HOA</a></li><li><a href="#city" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">City limits</a></li><li><a href="#flood" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood zone</a></li><li><a href="#the-landing" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The Landing</a></li><li><a href="#plantation-point-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Plantation Point FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="life"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Life here">What is it like to live in Plantation Point?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county's map shows an in-ground pool at 176 of the 352 houses here. Across Horry County, the same map shows about 1 in-ground pool for every 16 residential buildings. Our <a href="/buyers/pool-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">pool homes guide</a> covers what a pool costs to keep.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-d/plantation-point/plantation-point-pools-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-d/plantation-point/plantation-point-pools-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-d/plantation-point/plantation-point-pools-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of part of Plantation Point in Myrtle Beach: large houses on wooded lots along curving streets, many with a blue in-ground pool behind the house" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Part of Plantation Point from the air. The bright blue shapes behind the houses are in-ground pools.</figcaption></figure><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><style>main#main .hx-qs{margin:1rem 0 1.4rem}main#main .hx-strip.hx-qs:empty{display:block!important;height:0;margin:0;overflow:hidden}</style><script>(function(){function fill(s){if(s.getAttribute("data-done"))return;s.setAttribute("data-done","1");fetch("/homes/api/strip?"+s.getAttribute("data-q"),{credentials:"same-origin"}).then(function(r){return r.ok?r.json():null}).then(function(j){if(!j||!j.ok||!j.html||j.html.indexOf("hx-s-empty")>-1)return;var hd=document.createElement("p");hd.className="hx-s-head";var b=document.createElement("b");b.textContent=s.getAttribute("data-head");hd.appendChild(b);if(j.link&&j.link.charAt(0)==="/"){var a=document.createElement("a");a.href=j.link;a.textContent="See all";hd.appendChild(a)}var row=document.createElement("div");row.className="hx-s-row";row.innerHTML=j.html;s.appendChild(hd);s.appendChild(row);if(j.note){var n=document.createElement("p");n.className="hx-s-note";n.textContent=j.note;s.insertBefore(n,row)}}).catch(function(){})}function go(){var all=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll(".hx-qs[data-q]"));if(!("IntersectionObserver" in window)){all.forEach(fill);return}var io=new IntersectionObserver(function(es){es.forEach(function(e){if(e.isIntersecting){io.unobserve(e.target);fill(e.target)}})},{rootMargin:"600px 0px"});all.forEach(function(s){io.observe(s)})}if(document.readyState==="loading")document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",go);else go()})();</script><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="subdivision=Plantation+Point&amp;has=pool" data-head="Plantation Point houses with their own pool"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Next door is Myrtlewood Golf Club, with two courses, PineHills and Palmetto.</p><blockquote class="pp-quote">"PineHills is widely regarded as the soul of Myrtle Beach golf, and its Myrtlewood sister, the Palmetto Course, as the heart."<span><a href="https://www.playgolfmyrtlebeach.com/news/5-things-know-go-myrtlewood-pinehills/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Play Golf Myrtle Beach</a></span></blockquote><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The clubhouse is across the course, a 10-minute drive. Our <a href="/buyers/golf-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">golf communities guide</a> compares the area's golf neighborhoods.</p><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="subdivision=Plantation+Point&amp;has=on_golf_course" data-head="Plantation Point houses on the golf course"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical lot is about half an acre, and the smallest is about a third of an acre. The typical house is about 3,900 square feet under roof, garage included. The houses for sale this fall were built from 1987 to 2021.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most are full-time homes: the county taxes about 85 in 100 houses here as their owner's primary residence.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where a normal week takes you</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The nearest groceries are at the Food Lion in Plantation Point Plaza, across the bypass at 38th Avenue North.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Minutes by car from the middle of Plantation Point"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Minutes by car from the middle of Plantation Point</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Place</span><span role="columnheader">By car, about</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Broadway at the Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.467" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">7 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Food Lion, Plantation Point Plaza</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.533" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.6" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">9 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Coastal Grand Mall</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.733" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">11 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Grand Strand Medical Center</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.867" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">13 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach International Airport</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">15 min</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>With no traffic. The beach is the nearest public beach access, about 2.7 miles away, about an hour on foot. Routes on OpenStreetMap roads.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A little history</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach Farms</a>, formed in 1912 and later Burroughs & Chapin, played a central role in the growth of Myrtle Beach. It recorded Plantation Point's restrictions in phases, starting in 1990.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Several streets share their names with old rice plantations in Georgetown County, such as Annandale, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/94001236" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Hobcaw</a> and <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/71000782" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Hopsewee</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="lots"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Water and golf lots">Which Plantation Point lots are on the waterway and the golf course?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every waterway lot is in Plantation Point itself, and the map shows where they are. Two of the waterway houses sold in the past year, for $1.17 million and $1.9 million.</p><figure class="pp-fig"><div class="pp-frame"><svg class="pp-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1000 722" role="img" aria-labelledby="pp-map-t"><title id="pp-map-t">Map of Plantation Point in Myrtle Beach. The Intracoastal Waterway runs along one side, and the Myrtlewood golf courses along another. The lots on the waterway are blue, the lots on the golf course are green, and The Landing's smaller lots, near the US 17 Bypass, are tan. An arrow points southeast to the beach, 2.7 miles away by road.</title><rect width="1000" height="722" fill="#eef0e4"/><path d="M606.7 183.9L618 252.9L623.9 275.1L673.2 235.3L675.1 240.6L624.2 281.5L628.9 293.8L662.3 287.8L707.9 317.9L723.5 341.1L708.2 353.5L648.3 327.2L580.2 343L571.5 365.9L619.2 425.2L614.2 428.9L593.3 402.7L573 419.2L573.3 420.3L553.7 395.5L494.7 440.6L491.6 454.1L452.9 480L448.5 481.9L421.3 483.4L407 476.6L395.4 486L390.4 492.7L383 511.9L377 520.9L369.2 545.3L368.9 558.8L366.4 575.7L370.5 587.7L370.5 601.9L373.3 619.6L372 622.6L378.3 623.3L377 626.7L351.4 647.3L343 657.5L335.5 660.8L323 636.1L302.1 565.5L303.7 520.9L310.2 505.1L333.6 474.7L340.8 453.3L348.6 437.9L352.4 434.2L369.5 424.1L380.1 413.9L385.1 406.4L395.4 386.2L414.5 356.1L412.9 342.6L405.4 318.2L402.9 296.1L402.6 291.6L407.9 277L425.4 271L437.3 262.3L445.1 253.7L450.1 252.2L459.7 279.6L470.7 300.6L474.4 311.1L481.3 324.2L478.5 342.6L484.4 344.1L501.9 333.3L556.2 289.7L556.8 283L524.3 261.2L519.4 270.6L496.3 262.3L493.4 258.9L491.3 250.7L497.5 243.9L495.6 237.2L479.1 208.7L476.9 199.3L477.2 190.6L480.6 182L475.7 167.4L500.3 153.9L519 170.8L568.7 206.8L579.9 196.3L579 144.9L587.1 131L596.1 133.2L609.6 138.1L618.3 143L611.7 155.7L606.7 183.9ZM719.7 433.8L709.1 427.4L698.5 423.3L696.9 421.4L699.1 389.2L704.7 365.1L775.3 308.1L780.3 307.7L777.8 335.1L777.2 371.2L758.1 426.7L718.5 459L716 443.6L719.7 433.8ZM823.3 19.1L827.1 18.8L831.1 20.6L860.8 51L871.4 