"/><text class="sm" x="985" y="578" text-anchor="end">Beach, 2.7 mi</text></svg></div><ul class="pp-legend"><li><i style="background:#2f6f8f"></i>On the Intracoastal Waterway: 58 lots</li><li><i style="background:#5f8a4e"></i>On the golf course: 88 lots</li><li><i style="background:#e2b07f;border:3px solid #5f8a4e"></i>The Landing, with 47 lots on the course</li><li><i style="background:#ffffff"></i>Other lots in Plantation Point</li></ul><figcaption>Every lot in Plantation Point and The Landing. The arrow points to the nearest public beach access, 2.7 miles away by road. Lots: Horry County parcels. Roads: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line. Map: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Lots in both parts border the Myrtlewood courses. Empty lots are rare: the county map shows 14, and one on the course sold for $560,000 in the past year. The county zones these streets for single-family houses on lots of at least 10,000 square feet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you offer on a waterway house, we find out what dock it has and what the rules allow. Our <a href="/buyers/waterfront-homes/#docks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">waterfront homes guide</a> explains the dock rules on the Intracoastal.</p><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="subdivision=Plantation+Point" data-head="Every house for sale in Plantation Point"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">What do homes in Plantation Point sell for?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year 13 houses in Plantation Point sold, at a middle price of about $785,000. They ranged from about $375,000 to $1.9 million.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On November 13, 2026, 6 houses were for sale here, asking about $750,000 to $2.1 million.</p><p class="pp-note">Sale prices: Horry County deeds recorded in the past 12 months, houses only. Asking prices: CCMLS listings, counted in aggregate.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Besides the mortgage and <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">insurance</a>, property tax on a typical house here is about $2,900 a year as your <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">primary residence</a>. As a second home or rental it is about $9,500 a year. Most bills also include a flat county fee of about $90.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you own here and want to sell, our <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">home value page</a> explains how we price a home from recorded sales.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="hoa"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="HOA">Does Plantation Point have an HOA fee?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not one of the 6 Plantation Point homes for sale lists a monthly fee, and 3 of them say there is no HOA at all. Before you offer, we find out what the association collects, if anything, for the house you pick.</p><ul class="pp-rules one" aria-label="The HOA and the neighborhood's rules"><li><strong>The association</strong>The only parcel the county lists for Plantation Point HOA is a small common area by the US 17 Bypass.</li><li><strong>The fee shown for a home for sale</strong>The listing agent enters that fee, so we confirm it with the association.</li><li><strong>The recorded rules</strong>Each lot comes with recorded restrictions, the neighborhood's rules. The county's index of them is online, but the documents can only be read at the Register of Deeds in Conway. We pull them for the lot you like.</li><li><strong>Renting</strong>County zoning has no limit on how long a home outside the towns may be rented. A subdivision's recorded rules can have one. Our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules guide</a> covers renting by the night.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Like a lot? Have us pull its restrictions</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">We read the recorded rules for that lot in Conway and tell you what they allow before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=Plantation%20Point">Have us pull the restrictions</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="city"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City limits">Is Plantation Point in the City of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Every house here has a Myrtle Beach mailing address. The land is outside the city limits, in Horry County. Three things change for an owner:</p><ul class="pp-rules one" aria-label="What being outside the city limits changes"><li><strong>Property tax</strong>The bill has county and school tax and no city tax. The yearly figures above already count that.</li><li><strong>Trash</strong>The county does not collect trash at the curb. Owners hire a private hauler or use a county recycling and convenience center. The county's 25 centers are open only to residents outside the towns.</li><li><strong>City parking decal</strong>The city's resident parking decal is only for cars kept inside the city limits that pay city vehicle tax. Plantation Point owners do not qualify.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach guide</a> covers the city's own neighborhoods and what changes inside its limits.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flood"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood zone">Is Plantation Point in a flood zone?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No house in Plantation Point or The Landing is in FEMA's high-risk zone, the zone where a lender requires flood insurance. We checked every house outline here against FEMA's map.</p><ul class="pp-rules one" aria-label="What the flood map shows here"><li><strong>Along the water</strong>A high-risk strip runs along the Intracoastal. It touches the waterway edge of 35 lots and stops short of the houses.</li><li><strong>Flood history</strong>A zone does not show whether a house has flooded. We check each house's flood history before you offer. Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">flooding a seller may not mention</a> explains how.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Like a waterway house? Have us check its flood history</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We check its flood zone and its flood history, and tell you what we find.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=Plantation%20Point">Have us check a house</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="the-landing"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The Landing">The Landing at Plantation Point: the same location for less</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Landing at Plantation Point is the older, smaller part of the neighborhood, near the US 17 Bypass. Its houses sold for about $280,000 in the past year, about a third of Plantation Point's middle price.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It is the part closer to the beach, and the Food Lion is about 3 minutes away by car.</p><div class="pp-cmp"><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase"></th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Plantation Point</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">The Landing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Houses</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">352</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">139</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Lot</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Half an acre</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6,600&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Under roof</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">3,900&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,700&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Pools</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">176</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Golf lots</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">88</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">47</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Waterway lots</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">58</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">None</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Sold, past year</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">13, about $785,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">7, about $280,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Beach by car</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">9&nbsp;min</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6&nbsp;min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="pp-note">Sizes, prices and drives are the typical one for each part, rounded. Houses, lots and pools: Horry County parcels. Sales: deeds recorded in the past 12 months. Drives: no traffic.</p><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><div class="hx-strip" data-place="landing-at-plantation-point" data-name="The Landing at Plantation Point" data-head="The Landing at Plantation Point: 6 minutes to the beach"></div><div class="hx-strip hx-qs" data-q="near=33.72855%2C-78.88639&amp;miles=1" data-head="Homes for sale within a mile of Plantation Point"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="plantation-point-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Plantation Point FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is there a Plantation Point golf course?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The course beside the lots is Myrtlewood Golf Club, with two courses, PineHills and Palmetto. Lots in both Plantation Point and The Landing border it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where is Plantation Point Plaza?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Plantation Point Plaza is the shopping center at the US 17 Bypass and 38th Avenue North, with a Food Lion. It is about 8 minutes by car from the middle of Plantation Point and about 3 from The Landing.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you walk to the beach from Plantation Point?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not easily. The nearest public beach access is about 2.7 miles away, about an hour on foot or about 9 minutes by car.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I rent out a house in Plantation Point?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">County zoning has no limit on how long a home here may be rented. The recorded restrictions can have one, so we pull them for the house you pick.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I need flood insurance in Plantation Point?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No house here is in FEMA's high-risk zone, the zone where a lender requires flood insurance. Where the zone touches 35 lots along the water, it stops short of the houses, so we check each house's flood history before you offer.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">deed index</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/i0pfcm2o/appendix-b-zoning-ordinance-upated-912026.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">zoning</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood map</a>, <a href="https://www.playgolfmyrtlebeach.com/news/5-things-know-go-myrtlewood-pinehills/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtlewood</a>, <a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach Farms</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/94001236" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hobcaw</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/71000782" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hopsewee</a>, <a href="https://rivercrest.propertycapsule.com/web/property/49562478de4c54fafd4ec46fdb297de5-aa9ee5a5b1155137461f9e4c7389f038" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plantation Point Plaza</a>, <a href="https://www.solidwasteauthority.org/recyclingcenters.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">recycling centers</a>, <a href="https://www.solidwasteauthority.org/residential.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">trash pickup</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/apply_for/resident_parking_decal.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">parking decal</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenStreetMap</a>. Our counts: county parcels, building outlines, flood zones and the deed index. Listings: CCMLS, in aggregate. Drive